  FT["BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849"] = {"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":9,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"补充缴费养老金信托修正第 2 号命令 2024","en":"SUPPLEMENTAL CONTRIBUTORY PENSIONS TRUST AMENDMENT NO. 2 ORDER 2024","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 12/2024","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2024","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AMENDMENT-NO.-2-ORDER-2024.pdf》（5 页），本次切分 9 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AMENDMENT-NO.-2-ORDER-2024.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"and commencement"},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Supplemental Contributory Pensions Trust (Amendment) (No. 2) Order, 2024 and shall be deemed to have commenced on 13th April 2015."}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"of new sections 6A, 6B and 6C into S 58/2009"},"text":{"en":"The Supplemental Contributory Pensions Trust Order, 2009 is amended by the following three new sections immediately after section 6 - to examine persons 6A. (1) Without prejudice to section 6(3), an inspector or any of the referred to in section 6(2), in the course of an inspection under may examine orally any person supposed to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances of the case and shall reduce into writing any statement made by the person so examined.\n\n(2) Such person shall be legally bound to answer the questions relating to such case put to him by such inspector or any of the referred to in section 6(2), but may refuse to answer any question the answers to which would have a tendency to expose him to a criminal or to a penalty or forfeiture.\n\n(3) A statement made by any person under the provisions of this be read over to him and shall, after correction if necessary, be signed by him.\n\n(4) Any person who obstructs an inspector or any of the officers in this section is guilty of an offence. to assess contributions based on information available 6B. (1) An inspector may assess any contribution which is due by any based on any information available if the employer - (a} fails to prepare and keep any register or record any pertaining to each employee as required to be performed by him under this Order or any regulations or rules made or\n\n(b) fails or refuses to produce any contract of service, book of of salary, register and other document concerning each as required under this Order.\n\n(2) The assessment made under subsection (1) shall be sufficient of the Board's claim for the summary recovery of any contribution section 38. of Managing Director to require information and application for search warrant 6C. (1) For the purposes of obtaining full information for ascertaining any person is liable to pay contributions under this Order, the Director may, by notice in writing, require any person(a} to furnish the Managing Director within a time specified in the notice not being less than 30 days from the date of such notice any or particulars specified in the notice;\n\n(b) to attend personally before the Managing Director or any authorised in that behalf by the Managing Director and for examination all books, accounts, records and other which the Managing Director or authorised officer deems or\n\n(c) to furnish the information or particulars in accordance with (a} and also to attend in accordance with paragraph (b).\n\n(2) Where a person is found guilty of an offence under\n\n(4)(a}, the court before which the person is found guilty shall such person to comply with the notice of the Managing .Director under\n\n(1) within 21 days from the date of the order of the court.\n\n(3) Whenever it appears to any court, upon written information on oath, and after any enquiry it may think necessary, that there are reasonable for suspecting that there are on particular premises any book, record or other document the production of which has been pursuant to subsection (1) and which has not been produced in with that requirement, such court may issue a warrant the Managing Director or any person named therein with or assistance - fa) to search the premises and to break open and search any drawer, chest, trunk, box, package or other receptacle, a fixture or not, in the premises; and {b) to take possession of, or secure against interference, any record or other document that appears to be the book, record or other document the production of which was so\n\n(4) Any person who - fa) fails to comply with subsection (1); or {b) obstructs the Managing Director or any person named referred to in subsection (3), of an offence.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"of section 12"},"text":{"en":"12 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (1), by \"8\" from the second line and by substituting \"10\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"of section 18"},"text":{"en":"of the principal Order is amended - {a) in subsection (2){b), by deleting \"amanah\" and by substituting • Amanah\" {b) by deleting \"person\" and by substituting \"member\" wherever the word"}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"of section 28"},"text":{"en":"of the principal Order is repealed and the following new section is therefor - \"Offences by bodies corporate etc."}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"heading":{"en":"of section 29"},"text":{"en":"the principal Order is amended, in subsection (2), by deleting \"may\" from the first line and by substituting \"shall\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"heading":{"en":"of new section 38A"},"text":{"en":"The principal Order is amended by inserting the following new section after section 38 - \"Joint and several liability on directors etc. 38A. (1) Where any contribution remaining unpaid by a body corporate, association or body of persons, then, notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this Order or any other written law, the directors or directors of such body corporate, or the partners or former partners of such partnership, or the members of such association or body of persons or the office bearers of such association or body of persons, as the case may be, during such period in which contributions were liable to be paid, shall with the body corporate, partnership, association or body of liable to pay contributions, be jointly and severally liable for the due and payable to the Trust.\n\n(2) In this section, \"contributions\" includes any dividend, service and penalty on any contribution charged by the Board under this or any regulations or rules made thereunder.\". of section 39"}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (3), in {a}, by inserting\", including by electronic or other means\" immediately \"thereto\". Made this 11th. day of Rejab, 1445 Hijriah corresponding to the 23rd. day of January, 2024 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Darussalam.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN, DARUSSALAM."}},{"id":"BN-S-12-2024-SUPPLEMENTAL-CONTRIBUTORY-PENSIONS-TRUST-AM-7FE849-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28."},"text":{"en":"an offence against this Order or any regulations or rules made committed by a body corporate, partnership, association or other body of persons is proved to have been committed with the consent or of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of any manager, secretary or other similar officer of that body corporate, association or other body of persons, or any person who was to act in that capacity, he as well as that body corporate, association or other body of persons is guilty of that offence and to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.\"."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"SUPPLEMENTAL CONTRIBUTORY PENSIONS TRUST AMENDMENT NO. 2 ORDER 2024","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000"] = {"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":10,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"紧急消防服务法修正命令 2000","en":"EMERGENCY FIRE SERVICE ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 2000","orig":null},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"S 13/2000","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2000","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-13_2000_E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000.pdf》（7 页），本次切分 10 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-13_2000_E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Emergency Wire Service Act) Citation. (Amendment) Order, 2000."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"Act, is amended -section 7 of"},"text":{"en":"Section 7 of the Fire Service Act, in this Order referred to as the Amendment of Chapter 82. fa) in paragraph (a), by inserting \", fighting, preventing and controlling:' immediately after \"extinguishing\";\n\n(b) by deleting paragraph (c) and by substituting the following new paragraphs therefor - \"(c) the prevention of fire;\n\n(d) investigating into the cause, origin and circumstances of fires;\n\n(e) performing humanitarian services, including the protection of life and property in any calamity; m giving advice on fire protection measures and fire hazards;\n\n(g) executing such other duties as may be imposed on them.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"Section 8 of the Act is amended in paragraph (c), by inserting Amendment"},"text":{"en":"Section 8 of the Act is amended in paragraph (c), by inserting Amendment \"or for preventing the spread of the fire\" immediately after \"fire\" in of section 8. the last line."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"sections immediately after section 8 -of new"},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following three new Insertion sections SA, 88 and 8C. \"Emergencies 8A. On the occasion of an emergency not involving not involving fire or the risk of fire, the powers referred to in sections fire. 7 and 8 slj_all be exercised by any member if he is of the opinion that life or property are in imminent danger. Power to 8B. (1) The Director and any member authorised by investigate. him in writing shall have the power to investigate the commission of any offence under this Act or any regulations made thereunder.\n\n(2) Every person required by the Director or such authorised member to give information or produce any document or other article relating to the commission of any such offence which is in that person's power to give shall be legally bound to give the information or to produce the document or other article.\n\n(3) Nothing in this section affects any power of any police officer. Powers of 8C. (1) The Director, any member authorised by him arrest and in writing, and any police officer may without a warrant search. arrest any person whom he reasonably suspects to have committed an offence punishable under this Act or any regulations made thereunder {a} if the name and address of that person are unknown to him; {b) if that person declines to give his name and address; {c) if there is any reason to doubt the accuracy of the name and address, if given; or {d) if in his opinion he is likely to abscond.\n\n(2) A person arrested under this section may be detained until his name and address have been correctly ascertained.\n\n(3) No person so arrested shall be detained longer than is necessary for bringing him before a court, unless the order of a court for his detention has been obtained. 14) Any member authorised by the Director in writing and any police officer may without a warrant and with or without assistance stop and search any person, whether in a public place or not, if he has reason to believe that any evidence of the commission of an offence against this Act or regulations made thereunder is likely to be found on such person and may seize any evidence so found.\n\n(5) No women shall be searched under subsection (4) except by a woman.\". Amendment 5. Section 14 of the Act is amendedof section 14. {a} in subsection (1), by inserting \"and Fire Service Standing Orders\" immediately before \"not\" in the second line; {b} in paragraph {b} of subsection (2), by adding \"and the regulation and carrying out of punishment\"; {c} by repealing paragraph (1) of subsection (2) and by substituting the following new paragraphs therefor - \"{l} instructions and examinations; {m} Fire Service duties of every description and the manner in which they shall be carried out; {n} the institution and maintenance of messes, canteens, reading rooms and sports organisation; {o} the control and use of all Fire Service equipment; {p} transfers of members, the places at which they shall reside and the particular services to be performed by them; {q} such other matters as may be necessary or expedient for preventing abuse or neglect of duty, for rendering the Fire Service efficient in the discharge of its duties and for carrying out the objects of this Act.\". Amendment 6. Section 15 of the Act is amended of section 15. {a} by inserting \"or loss suffered in consequence of any action taken or work done\" immediately after \"done\" in the fi.rst line; and {b} by inserting \"or powers\" immediately after \"duties\" in the second line."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"heading":{"en":"Section 16 of the Act is amended by adding \"or any calamity\". Amendment"},"text":{"en":"Section 16 of the Act is amended by adding \"or any calamity\". Amendment of section 16."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"heading":{"en":"Section 17 of the Act is amended Amendment"},"text":{"en":"Section 17 of the Act is amended Amendment of section 17.\n\n(a) in subsection 11), by deleting \"or business or vessel specifier! by the applicant\" from the last two lines and by substituting therefor \", business, vessels, vehicle, aircraft or any moveable structures specified by the applicant and, for the purpose, furnish such equipment as he may deem necessary\"; and {b) in subsection (2), by inserting \"and for the use of equipment so furnished\" immediately after \"detailed\" in the second line."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"heading":{"en":"immedately after section 17 -of new"},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section Insertion section 17 A. \"Fees. 17 A. The fees specified in the Fourth Schedule shall be Fourth paid in respect of the matters to which they relate.\". Schedule."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"heading":{"en":"Section 18 of the Act is repealed and the following new section Substitution"},"text":{"en":"Section 18 of the Act is repealed and the following new section Substitution substituted therefor -of section 18. Regulations. 18. (1) The Minister, with the approval of His II Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, may make regulations generally for carrying into effect the objeQts and purposes of this Act, including the prescription of fees, and for the due administration thereof. 12) Such regulations may make different provision as respects different classes of case to which they apply, and may include such incidental, consequential and supplementary provisions as the Minister considers necessary or expedient.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"heading":{"en":"Section 19 of the Act is repealed a.nd the following new section Substitution"},"text":{"en":"Section 19 of the Act is repealed a.nd the following new section Substitution substituted therefor -of section 19. Amendment, 19. The provisions contained in any Schedule may be etc., II of amended, cancelled or replaced by regulations made by Schedules. the Minister with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan.\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2000-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-SERVICE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2000-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"heading":{"en":"Section 20 of the Act is amended -Amendment"},"text":{"en":"Section 20 of the Act is amended -Amendment of section 20. (a} by deleting \"of $1,200 and imprisonment for 6 months\" from the last two lines of subsection ( 1) and by substituting \"not exceeding $6,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or both\" therefor;\n\n(b) by adding the following two new subsections\"(4) No prosecution for any offence punishable under this Act or any regulations made thereunder shall be instituted except with the written sanction of the Public Prosecutor.\n\n(5) Prosecutions for offences punishable under this Act or any such regulations may be conducted by a member authorised in writing in that behalf by the Public Prosecutor.\". Insertion of 13. The Act is amended by inserting the following new section new section 21. immediately after section 20 - \"Application of 21. The provisions of this Act apply, subject to such Act and modifications as may be prescribed, to - regulations to vessels,· etc. (a} vessels remaining moored or on dry land, for such periods or in such circumstances as may be prescribed;\n\n(b) tents and other movable structures; {c) vessels or boats afloat or travelling within Brunei Darussalam;\n\n(d) any buildings built along a river.\". Addition of 14. The Act is amended by adding the following new Schedule - Fourth Schedule. \"FOURTH SCHEDULE jsection 17 A) FEES A. On registration of plans submitted: $5.00 each B. On processing and approval of new, resubmitted, altered or amended plans: Private dwelling house plan (bungalows, terrace houses, detached and semi-detached houses) $15.00 per unit Architectural, mechanical, electrical and fire-protection plans (commercial, factories, flats, hotels, offices and $50.00 per storey others) per building C. Inspection, testing and checking of fire-fighting equipment, per time: Automatic sprinkler $150.00 per system Wet riser $100.00 per system Dry riser $150.00 per system Fire-hose reel $50.00 per system Automatic detection system $100.00 per system Manual break-glass callpoint $50.00 per system · Portable fire extinguisher (excluding refill) $1.00 each Fixed installation system (C02, FM200, Inergen and others) $100.00 per system Smoke spill system $100.00 per system Firemen lifts $50.00 each Fire hydrant $15.00 each Firemen intercom communication system in a building $50.00 per system Fire dampers $10.00 each Fire door $1.00 each Standby generator $25.00 per system Emergency lighting and Exit $5.00 per storey signs per building Pressurised staircase $50.00 per system LPG (Liquefied Petroleum Gas) piping and/or Chlorination system $50.00 per system Escalator $50.00 per system Fire shutters $50.00 per building.\". IYfade this 20th. day of Syawal, 1420 Hijriah corresponding to the 27th. day of January, 2000 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM"}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"EMERGENCY FIRE SERVICE ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 2000","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001"] = {"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":16,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"广播类别执照公告 2001","en":"BROADCASTING CLASS LICENCE NOTIFICATION 2001","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 13/2001","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2001","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001.pdf》（7 页），本次切分 16 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"This Notification may be cited as the Broadcasting (Class Licence!"},"text":{"en":"In this Schedule - \"licensee\" means a person who provides a licensable broadcasting service that is subject to a class licence under section 12 of the Act; \"newspaper\" means any publication containing news, intelligence, reports of occurrences, or any remarks, observations or comments and published in any form, for sale or free distribution, at regular intervals or otherwise, but does not include any publication published by or for the Government; \"service\" means a licensable broadcasting service that is subject to a class licence under section 12 of the Act."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"\"Internet Content Provider\" means"},"text":{"en":"(1) An Internet Service Provider shall{a) register with the Minister within 14 days of 12th. February, 2001, or in the case of an Internet Service Provider who provides the service after 12th. February, 2001, within 14 days of providing the service; {b) faithfully and truthfully furnish such information, and furnish such undertakings, as the Minister may require in connection with the provision of the Internet Service Provider's service; and {c) pay the following licence fees -\n\n(i) for the provision of a computer on-line service by an Internet Access Service Provider, $1,000 per annum;\n\n(ii) for the provision of a computer on-line service by a Nonlocalised Internet Service Reseller:, $250 per annum; and\n\n(iii) for the provision of a computer on-line service by a Localised Internet Service Reseller, $250 per annum for each premises at which the computer on-line services are provided.\n\n(2) Sub-paragraph (1} does not apply to a Localised Internet Service Reseller who, in the opinion of the Minister, provides Internet services(a} (a) for purposes only incidental to its primary business; or\n\n(b) for purposes of demonstration only on an occasional basis."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"a class licence"},"text":{"en":"An Internet Content Provider who is or is determined by the Minister to be - (a} a political party registered in Brunei Darussalam providing any programme on the World Wide Web through the Internet; or (b} a body of persons engaged in the propagation, promotion or discussion of political or religious issues relating to Brunei Darussalam on the World Wide Web through the Internet, shall register with the Minister within 14 days of 12th. February, 2001 or, in the case of an Internet Content Provider who provides the service after 12th. February, 2001, within 14 days after the commencement of its service, or within such longer time as the Minister may permit."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"The conditions of the class licence referred to in paragraph 3 are set out in the"},"text":{"en":"If required hy the Minister to do so by notice in writing - (a} an Internet Conte11t Provider who is, or is determined by the Minister to be, in the business of providing through the Internet an on-line newspaper; and (b} an Internet Content Provider who is, or is determined by the Minister to be, an individual providing any programme, for the propagation, promotion or discussion of political or religious issues relating to Brunei Darussalam, qn the World Wide Web through the internet, shall register with the Minister within the time stipulated by the Minister in the notice."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"provision of any licensable broadcasting service that is subject to a class licence"},"text":{"en":"An Internet Content Provider who is required to register under paragraph 3 or 4 shall faithfully and truthfully furnish such information, and furnish such undertakings, as the Minister may require in connection with the provision of the Internet Content Provider's service."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"A licensee who is required to register with the Minister under paragraph 2, 3 or 4 shall give the Minister 14 days written notice of its intention to terminate the provision of its service,"}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"A licensee shall at all times comply with the laws of Brunei Darussalam."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"A licensee shall {a) assist the Minister in the investigation into - (il any breach of its licence; or\n\n(ii) any alleged violation of anv law committed by the licensee or any other person; and\n\n(b) produce such information, re:::ords, documents, data or other materials as may be required by the Minister for the purpose of the investigation."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"A licensee who intends to broadcast its service on(a) a radio frequency;\n\n(b) any spare capacity or sub-carrier on a television or radio channel; or\n\n(c) television lines in the Vertical Blanking Interval, shall, before the comme~1cement of the broadcast of its service, inform the Minister of its intention to broadcast its service by such means and obtain such approvals as the Minister may direct for the broadcast of its service by such means."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"The licensee shall keep and furnish to the Minister all information, records, documents, data or other materials concerning or relating to the provision of its service as the Minister may, from time to time, require."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"A licensee shall use its best efforts to ensure that its service -\n\n(a) complies with such Codes of Practice as the Minister may issue from time to time; and\n\n(b) is not used for any purpose, and does not contain any programme, that(i) is against the public interest, public order or national harmony; or\n\n(ii) offends against good taste or decency."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"An Internet Content Provider who provides a webpage on the World Wide Web through the Internet to which other persons are invited to contribute or post programmes shall use its best efforts to ensure that such programmes conform with such applicable Codes of Practice as the Minister may issue from time to time."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"A licensee who provides any licensable broadcasting service referred to in paragraph 3{a) to {b) of this Notification, shall {a) ensure that its service is not used for, or in furtherance of, games and lotteries, the conduct of which is an offence under the Common Gaming Houses Act (Chapter 28) unless the licensee is exempted from the provisions of that Act; {b) ensure that its service 1s not used to advertise, provide or otherwise promote(i) any religion other than Islam;\n\n(ii) any practice proscribed by the teachings of Islam; {c) ensure that its service is not used for the solicitation of prostitution or for any other immoral activity; {d) ensure that any professional advice, or any specialist consultancy service, offered on its service is offered by persons with qualifications recognised by the relevant professional bodies in Brunei Darussalam; {e) in the case of the broadcast of sound recordings, ensure that only sound recordings that are acceptable to the Minister are broadcast; and {f) in the case of the broadcast of films or video recordings, ensure that only films and video recordings that are approved by the Panel of Censors are broadcast, unless the film or video recording is one to which the Censorship of Films and Public Entertainments Act (Chapter 69) does not apply or is one which is exempted from the provisions of that Act."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"text":{"en":"A licensee shall remove, or prohibit the broadcast of, the whole or any part of a programme included in its service if the Minister informs the licensee that the broadcast of - {a) the whole or part of the programme is contrary to a Code of Practice applicable to the licen,see; or {b) the programme(i) is against the public interest, public order or national harmony; or\n\n(ii) offends against good taste or decency."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"text":{"en":"If any doubt arises as to whether a licensee has used its best efforts in compliance with the conditions of its licence, the licensee shall be treated as having used its best efforts if it satisfied the Minister that it took all reasonable steps in the circumstances."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2001-BROADCASTING-CLASS-LICENCE-NOTIFICATION-2001-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"text":{"en":"Nothing in this Schedule shall exempt the licensee from complying with the requirements of any other written law relating to the provision of the licensee's service. Made this 9th. day of Zulkaedah, 1421 Hijriah corresponding to the 3rd. day of February, 2001. PEHIN ORANG KAYA LAlLA SETIA BAKTI DIRAJA DATO LAlLA UTAMA HAJI AWANG ISA BIN PEHIN DATU PERDANA MANTER! DATO LAlLA UTAMA HAJI IBRAHIM Minister responsible for broadcasting matters, Prime Minister's Office, Brunei Darussalam."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"BROADCASTING CLASS LICENCE NOTIFICATION 2001","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-13-2003-E-AITI-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2003"] = {"id":"BN-S-13-2003-E-AITI-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2003","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"文莱达鲁萨兰国 AITI 修正命令 2003","en":"AITI OF BRUNEI DARUSSALAM AMENDMENT ORDER 2003","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 13/2003","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2003","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-13_2003_E-AITI-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2003.pdf》（1 页），本次切分 2 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-13_2003_E-AITI-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2003.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-13-2003-E-AITI-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2003-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Authority for Info-communications Technology Industry of Brunei Darussalam (Amendment) Order, 2003. Amendment of Third Schedule to S 39/01."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2003-E-AITI-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2003-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The Authority for Info-communications Technology Industry of Brunei Darussalam Order, 2001 i~ amended, in the Third Schedule, by repealing paragraphs 3 and 4 and by substituting the following new paragraph therefor - \"3. The accounts of the Authority shall be audited annually by (a} the Auditor General; or\n\n(b) any person who has been authorised to perform the duties required by the Companies Act (Chapter 39) to be performed by an auditor, who sh-h.ll be appointed annually by the Minister in consultation with the Auditor General: Provided that where the accounts of the Authority have been audited by a person appointed under paragraph (b), they may be verified by the Auditor General before a copy thereof is submitted to the Minister pursuant to paragraph 13.\". Made this 21st. day of Muharam, 1424 Hijriah corresponding to the 24th. day of March, 2003 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM"}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"AITI OF BRUNEI DARUSSALAM AMENDMENT ORDER 2003","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18"] = {"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":24,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"证据法第二号修正命令 2006 第 18 条","en":"VIDENCE ACT AMENDMENT NO. 2 ORDER 2006 SEC 18","orig":null},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"S 13/2006","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2006","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO.-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18.pdf》（13 页），本次切分 24 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO.-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Evidence Act (Amendment) (No. 2) Order,"}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"This Order applies to all proceedings, including proceedings instituted before the commencement of this Order. of section 3 of Chapter 108."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"Section 3 of the Evidence Act, in this Order referred to as the Act, is {a) by deleting the defmition of \"document\" and by substituting the new definition therefor - means any matter expressed, described or howsoever upon any substance, material, thing or article, including any matter embodied in a disc, tape, film, soundtrack or other device by means of - {a) letters, figures, marks, symbols, signals or other forms of description or representation whatsoever;\n\n(b) any visual recording (whether of still or moving images);\n\n(c) any sound recording or any electronic, magnetic, mechanical or other recording, whatsoever and howsoever made, or any electronic impulse or other data whatsoever;\n\n(d) a recording or transmission of the means mentioned in (a}, (b) or (c), or by more than one of the means in paragraph (a), (b}, {c) or (d), intended to be used or which may be used for the purpose of expressing, or howsoever representing that matter; A writing is a document. Words printed, lithographed or photographed are documents. A map, plan, graph or sketch is a document. on wood, metal, stone or any other substance, material or thing is a document. A photograph or a negative is a document. A tape recording of a telephonic communication, including a recording of such communication transmitted over distance is a document. or other visual recording, including a recording of or other visual transmission over a distance is a document. A matter recorded, stored, processed, retrieved or produced by a is a document.\"; {b) by adding the following three new definitions'\"'film\" includes a microfilm and any negative; means any transparent material bearing a visual image in size either singly or as a series, and includes microfiche; means a transparent negative photograph on any substance or material, and includes any transparent negative photograph made from the original negative photograph.\". of section 32."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":". Section 32 of the Act is amended - {a} by inserting \"(ll\" immediately before \"Statements\" in the first line; {b) by substituting a semicolon for the fullstop at the end of paragraph {h) and by inserting the following new paragraph immediately thereafter - \"{i} when the statement was made in the course of, or for the purposes of, any investigaton or inquiry into an offence under or by virtue of any law; and such statement was made by a public officer in the of his duties.\";\n\n(c) by adding the following new subsection \"(2) The provisions of paragraph (i) shall apply only in relation to a criminal proceeding.\". of section 35A."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"Section 35A is amended, in subsection (1), by deleting \"computere\" from the second line and by substituting \"computer\" therefor. new section 35C."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after 5B - 35A and 35B to prevail over the provisions of Act and any written law. 35C. The provisions of sections 35A and 35B shall prevail and have full and effect notwithstanding anything inconsistent therewith or contrary thereto contained in this Act or in any other written law relating to certification, production, admission or proof of evidence in any criminal or civil proceeding.\". of section 60."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"Section 60 of the Act is amended, in subsection (3) -\n\n(a) by deleting \"other than\" from the second line and by substituting \"including\" therefor;\n\n(b) by inserting \"or other document\" immediately after 11thing\" in the last line. of new section 60A."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after through live video or live television links. 60A. (1} Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, a person may, with leave of the court, give evidence through a live video or live television link in any proceedings if the court is satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice to do so. {2) The court may, in granting leave under subsection (1), make an on all or any of the following matters - (aj the persons who may be present at the place where the witness is giving evidence; (bJ that a person be excluded from the place while the witness is (cJ the persons in the courtroom who must be able to be heard, and heard, by the witness and by the persons with the witness; (dJ the persons in the courtroom who must not be able to be or seen and heard, by the witness and by the persons with the (eJ the persons in the courtroom who must be able to see and hear the witness and the persons with the witness; (fJ the stages in the proceedings during which a specified part of the order is to have effect; (gJ any other order the court considers necessary in the interests of justice.\n\n(3) Evidence given by a witness, whether in Brunei Darussalam or elsewhere, through a live video or live television link by virtue of this section or of any other written law shall be deemed for the purposes of sections 193, and 209 of the Penal Code (Chapter 22) as having been the proceedings in which it is given.\n\n(4) Where a witness gives evidence in accordance with this section or written law, he shall, for the purposes of this Act, be deemed to be . giving evidence in the presence of the court.\". of section 62."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"Section 62 of the Act is amended by inserting the following new Explanation immediately after Explanation 2 - 3 -A document produced by a computer is primary evidence.\". of section 63."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"Section 63 in the Act is amended, in paragraph (eJ, by deleting \"it\" and by substituting \"or heard it or perceived it by whatever means\" therefor. of new section 68A."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after \"Manner of giving voluminous or complex evidence. 68A. Ill Evidence may be given in the form of charts, summaries, output or other explanatory material if it appears to the court that fa} the would be to aid the court's comprehension of other evidence which is relevant and admissible according to the provisions of this Act or any other written law; and· fbJ the evidence that is to be given by any party is so voluminous or complex that the court considers it convenient to assess the evidence by reference to such material. (2l Any fact or opinion asserted in any material referred to in Ill shall be proved by relevant and admissible evidence, and if such fact or opinion is one that is admissible only on the proof of some other fact or opinion, such last-mentioned fact or opinion must be proved before evidence is given of the first-mentioned fact or opinion, unless the party so asserting undertakes to give proof of such fact or opinion and the court is with such undertaking. l3l In any proceedings where any material referred to in subsection\n\n(1) is adduced in evidence, the court mayfa} direct the party to provide such material in any form, the computer output; fbJ require the provision of such material or a copy thereof, including the identity and address of the person who prepared the the other parties; and fcJ specify a period within which such material or a copy thereof shall be provided to all parties to the proceedings.\". of new section 78A."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after in criminal proceedings in respect of foreign documents. 78A. (1) Any document purporting to be signed by the Attorney General that any foreign document attached thereto has been received by him in connection with any criminal proceedings shall be admitted in evidence in those proceedings together with the document attached thereto on production, without further proof, as prima facie evidence of the facts contained in such documents.\n\n(2) In this section, \"foreign document\" means a document purporting to be(a) a true copy or extract from(i) any record, book or document of a public nature kept or in any place outside Brunei Darussalam; or ·\n\n(ii) any document filed in or issued out of an office kept or in any place outside Brunei Darussalam for the purpose (whether the sole purpose or not) of registering companies or business names or the of property; and\n\n(b) signed and certified as a true copy of or extract from any such record, book or document by a person having custody or control\n\n(3) In relation to a document tendered in evidence under this section and purporting to be signed and certified as a true copy of or extract from any record, book or document by a person having custody or control thereof, be presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that such record, book or is -\n\n(a) a record, book or document of a public nature kept or maintained in a place outside Brunei Darussalam; or\n\n(b) a document filed in or issued out of an office kept or in a place outside Brunei Darussalam for the purpose of registering companies or business names or the ownership of property, if there is endorsed on the document a statement purporting to be signed by that person to that effect.\n\n(4) the court otherwise orders, a document shall not be admitted in evidence under this section unless 14 days notice in writing of the intention to tender such document in evidence, together with a copy thereof and of the certificate under subsection ( 1) of the Attorney General in respect thereof, has been served(a} where the document is tendered by the prosecution, on the (or, if more than one, on each defendant) or his counsel;\n\n(b) where the document is tendered by a defendant, on the Public Prosecutor, but nothing in this subsection shall affect the admissibility of a document in which notice has not been served in accordance with the requirements of this subsection if no person entitled to be so served objects to its being so of section 83."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"Section 83 of the Act is amended by - (a} deleting (I) immediately before \"The\" in the first line;\n\n(b) repealing subsection (2). of section 90."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"text":{"en":"Section 90 of the Act is amended by deleting \"30\" from the first line and by substituting \"20\" therefor. of section 113."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"text":{"en":"Section 113 of the Act is repealed. of section 123."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"text":{"en":"Section 123 of the Act is repealed and the following new section substituted as to affairs of State."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by adding the following new Chapter - XIII Records Interpretation of this Chapter."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18."},"text":{"en":"The Bankers' Books (Evidence) Act is repealed. Made this 13th. day of Muharam, 1427 Hijriah corresponding to the 12th. day of February, 2006 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM"}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A123","no":123,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 123."},"text":{"en":"Notwithstanding any other law on the contrary, no one shall be permitted to produce any unpublished official records relating to affairs of any document in the possession of a Ministry or of a department of Government, or to give any evidence derived therefrom, except with the the Permanent Secretary of the Ministry or the head of the concerned, who shall give or withhold such permission as he f:tt, subject however to the control of the Minister concerned, and no court shall order the production of any such record or document until such permission has been obtained.\". of new Chapter XIII."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A176","no":176,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 176."},"text":{"en":"In this Chapter - \"bank\" and \"banker\" mean any company carrying on the business of banking in Brunei Darussalam under a licence granted under any law relating to banking; 11 includes - {a} any document or record received or used in the ordinary business of a bank; and {b} any record so used which is kept otherwise than in a legible form and is capable of being reproduced in a legible form; \"Minister of Finance\" includes the Permanent Secretary of the Ministry . Copy of entry in banker's record."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A177","no":177,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 177."},"text":{"en":"(1) Subject to this section, a copy of any entry or matter recorded in a banker's record shall, on its production without further proof, be admitted in any proceedings as prima facie evidence of the matters, transactions and accounts therein recorded if {a} it is proved(i) that such entry was made or matter recorded m the ordinary course of business; and\n\n(ii) that such record is in the custody or control of the bank; and {b) except in the case of a copy made by any photographic and subject to subsection (3), it is proved by some person who the copy with the original entry, that the copy has been with the original entry and is correct.\n\n(2) A bank or officer of a bank shall not, in any proceedings other than proceedings instituted by or against the bank, be compelled to produce any banker's record the contents of which can be proved under this section, or to appear as a witness to prove the matters, transactions or accounts therein recorded, except - {a) in civil proceedings, by order of a judge made for special cause; {b) in criminal proceedings, by order of the court of trial.\n\n(3) banker's record kept by means of a computer, it not be necessary to prove· the matters referred to in paragraph {b) of\n\n(1) in relation to a document produced by the computer which is in evidence under this section as a copy of a matter recorded therein if it is proved - {a) that the document was so produced under the direction of a person having practical knowledge of and experience in the use of means of storing, processing or retrieving information; {b) that during the period when the computer was used for the of keeping such record, appropriate measures were in force for preventing unauthorised interference with the computer; and {c) that during the period, and at the time that the document was produced by the computer, the computer was operating properly that any respect in which it was not operating properly or was out of operation was not such as to affect the production of the or the accuracy of its contents. and in this subsection \"cm;nputer\" has the same meaning as in subsection (8)\n\n(4) In any proceedings, the matters referred to in paragraphs {a) and {b) of subsection (1) and in paragraphs {a), {b) and {c) of subsection (3) in banker's record may be proved, orally or by affidavit, by any the bank, and any such affidavit shall, on its production without proof, be admitted in evidence and may include an explanation of the of the copy of any entry or matter recorded in such banker's record is tendered in evidence or any abbreviations, symbols or other markings appearing in such copy that may be relevant in the proceedings, --------------------------------------------------~ and a description of the banker's record, its nature and use, and the procedures followed in keeping it; and for the purposes of this subsection it be sufficient for a matter referred to in paragraph {a)(i) of subsection ( 1) or in paragraph (c} of subsection (3) to be stated in an affidavit to the best of the knowledge and belief of the person making the affidavit.\n\n(5) In relation to any criminal proceedings, this section shall apply to any document or record used in the ordinary business of a body designated by the Minister of Finance under section 179 for the purposes of such criminal proceedings as it applies to a banker's record, and a reference in bank shalC in its application 'to such document or record, be construed as a reference to the body so designated. of section 177 to banks that have ceased business."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A178","no":178,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 178."},"text":{"en":"( 1) Section 177 shall apply to a copy of an entry or matter recorded in in the ordinary course of business of a former bank which is in evidence in criminal proceedings as it applies to a copy of an or matter recorded in a banker's record, but with the following (a} paragraph (a)(ii) of subsection ( 1) thereof shall be construed there were substituted \"any person duly authorised in that behalf or otherwise responsible for administering the affairs of the former bank\"; and {b} a reference therein to an officer of a bank shall, in relation to the former bank, be construed as a reference to any person who js, or is an officer of, a person responsible for administering the affairs of the\n\n(2) Section 177 shall apply to a copy of an entry or matter recorded in used in the ordinary course of business of a body designated by the · Minister of Finance under section 179 for the purposes of criminal which is tendered in evidence in those criminal proceedings as it applies to a copy of an entry or matter recorded in a banker's record, but with the following modifications - (a} a reference therein to a bank shall be construed as a person responsible for administering the affairs of that body; {b} a reference therein to an officer of a bank shall be construed any person who is, or is an officer of, a person responsible for administering the affairs of that boy.\n\n(3) In subsection (1), \"former bank\" means a bank which is being or has been wound up or dissolved or has otherwise ceased to carry on the business of banking. in criminal proceedings of designation of foreign bank."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A179","no":179,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 179."},"text":{"en":"(1} The Minister of Finance may, for the purposes of any criminal proceedings, designate any body formed or established outside Brunei which carries on the business of banking outside Brunei and a certificate purporting to be signed by the Minister of and certifying that any such body described therein has been him under this section for the purposes of those proceedings shall, on its production without further proof, be admitted m tho.se prima facie evidence of the facts contained therein.\n\n(2) The power conferred by subsection (1) may be exercised in any body formed or established outside Brunei Darussalam notwithstanding that it is being or has been wound up or dissolved or has otherwise ceased to carry on the business of banking. or judge may direct copies of entries in banker's record to be taken."}},{"id":"BN-S-13-2006-EVIDENCE-ACT-AMENDMENT-NO-2-ORDER-2006-SEC-18-A180","no":180,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 180."},"text":{"en":"(1) On the application of any party to any proceedings, the court or a order that such party be at liberty to inspect and take copies of any entries in a banker's record for any of the purposes of such proceedings. (2} An order under this section may be made either with or without the bank or any other party, and shall be served on the bank 3 clear days before the same is to be obeyed, unless the court or judge otherwise directs.\n\n(3) The costs of any application to the court or judge under or for the purposes of this section, and the costs of anything done or to be done under an order of the court or judge made under or for the purposes of this section, be in the discretion of the court or judge, who may order the same or any part thereof to be paid to any party by the bank, where the same have been occasioned by default or delay on the part of the bank.\n\n(4) Any such order against a bank may be enforced as if the bank were a party to the proceedings. n. of Chapter 107."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"VIDENCE ACT AMENDMENT NO. 2 ORDER 2006 SEC 18","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
