  FT["BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005"] = {"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":15,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"伊斯兰法庭修正命令 2005 第 13 条","en":"SEC 13 OF THE SYARIAH COURTS AMENDMENT ORDER 2005","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 17/2005","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2005","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005.pdf》（8 页），本次切分 15 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Syariah Courts Act (Amendment) Order, of section 2 of Chapter 184."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"Section 2 of the Syariah Courts Act, in this Order referred to as the Act, is by repealing subsection (3) and by substituting the following new subsection therefor - \"(3) If any conflict or doubt arises when interpreting any word or expression relating to Hukum Syara', the meaning of such word or expression shall be decided according to the accepted views (qaul muktamad) of the Mazhab Syafie.\". of new sections 7 A, 7B and 7C."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following 3 new sections immediately \"Sitting of Syariah Courts. 7A. (1) The Chief Syar'ie Judge may appoint such places as he thinks fit as houses for the Syariah Courts.\n\n(2) Any place in which a Syariah Court is held is deemed to be an open which the public generally may have access: that - (a} a Syariah Court shall have power to hear any proceeding or any part thereof in camera if the court is satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice, public security or propriety or for any other sufficient reason so to do; {b) a Syariah Court shall ordinarily exclude a witness until he has· given evidence in proceedings where the court is exercising a criminal [3) may at any time order that no person shall publish or photograph of any witness in any proceeding or any or any other thing liable to lead to the identi:&cation of any such and any person who acts in contravention of any such order shall, notwithstanding any other written law, be liable to a :&ne not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both. Subordinate officers. 7B. (1) There shall be attached to the Syariah Courts such interpreters, clerks, bailiffs, process-servers and other of:&cers as, from time to time, to the Chief Syar'ie Judge to be necessary for the administration of and the due execution of all powers and duties which are vested in the Syariah Courts.\n\n(2) Bailiffs, process-servers and any person generally or specially authorised by the Chief Syar'ie Judge to do so shall execute all writs, summonses, warrants, orders, notices and other mandatory processes of a Syariah Court given to them, and shall make a return of the same together with the manner of the execution thereof to the court from which the and shall arrest and receive all such persons and property as are committed to the custody of a Syariah Court.\n\n(3) A bailiff or other person in executing any writ of seizure and sale or any other writ of execution or of distress may effect an entry into any and for that purpose, if necessary, may break open any outer or door or window of the building or any receptacle therein, using such force as is reasonably necessary to effect an entry. and reasons. 7C. ( 1) A Syariah Court shall pronounce a decision at the conclusion of the hearing or at some time thereafter.\n\n(2) A Syariah Court may give reasons for its decision, if it so wishes, at the conclusion of the hearing or at any time thereafter.\n\n(3) The decision, and reasons if any, may be given orally or in writing.\n\n(4) Such decision, and reasons if any, may be sent to the parties and it shall not be necessary for them to appear in person or by counsel.\". of section 13."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"Section 13 of the Act is amended\n\n(a) in the sub-heading, by inserting \"Chief\" immediately after\n\n(b) by deleting 11Deputy Registrar and\" from the third line and by substituting \"Deputy Chief Registrar of the Syariah Appeal Court, .. therefor. of section 15."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"text":{"en":"Section 15 of the Act is amended by repealing paragraph (ix) and by substituting the following new paragraph therefor - \"(ix) determination of persons entitled to all or any part of the estate of a deceased Muslim and the parts thereof which such persons are respectively entitled to; or\". of section 16."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"Section 16 of the Act is amended, in paragraph (a) of subsection (1), by inserting \"and any written law relating to Islamic family law\" immediately before the comma in the second line. of new section 20A."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section immediatley after \"Appeals and applications for leave to appeal. 20A. (1) An appeal or application for leave to appeal under subsection (2) 20 shall be made to the Syariah Appeal Court in accordance with the prescribed procedure, but shall, in any case, be within 30 days from the date of the judgment, order or decision in respect of which the appeal or is made.\n\n(2) The Syariah Appeal Court, on hearing any application for leave to appeal may, on special ground, extend the period of appeal, notwithstanding that the time has expired.\". of new sections 21A and 21B."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following 2 new sections immediately \"No revision at instance of party who could have appealed. 21A. Where an appeal lies from any decision in any civil matter and no appeal is brought, no proceeding by way of revision shall be entertained at the instance of a party who could have appealed. Discretion of Syariah High Court or Syariah Appeal Court as to hearing parties. 21B. ( 1} the provisions of any written law, no party shall have any right to be heard before the Syariah High Court or the Syariah Appeal when exercising its powers of revision and supervision.\n\n(2) No final order shall be made to the prejudice of any person unless that person has had an opportunity of being so heard.\". of new section 24A."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after of Courts. 24A. For the purposes of and incidental to the hearing and determination of any appeal, the Syariah High Court and the Syariah Appeal Court, as the case may be, shall have the powers and jurisdiction of the court, person or tribunal from which or from whom the appeal was brought, in addition to may be conferred upon it by this Act or by any written law.\". of new section 27 A."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following new section immediately after of audience. 27 A. Subject to any written law which provides for syariah criminal in any proceeding in a Syariah Court, whether in the exercise of r its criminal or civil jurisdiction, any of the following may address the fa) any party to the proceedings; {b) any Syar'ie Lawyer and any person deemed to be a Syar'ie (cJ any other person allowed by leave of the court to appear instead of a party to the proceedings.\". section 28."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"text":{"en":"Section 28 of the Act is amended - {a) by inserting the following new paragraph immediately after {aJ\"faa) prescribing the scales of allowances, costs and fees to be taken, paid or refunded to any party or witness in any proceedings in the and to regulating any matters relating to the costs of such proceedings;\"; {bJ in paragraph {b), by deleting \"and\" from the last line; {cJ in paragraph {cJ, by deleting the fullstop and by substituting\";\" therefor;\n\n(d) by adding the following new paragraph - \"(dJ generally as he considers necessary or expedient for carrying into effect the provisions of this Act.\". of new sections 28A, 28B and 28C."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by inserting the following 3 new sections immediately 28A. Notwithstanding any other written law, where any contempt is the face of a Syariah Court, the court may at any time before the same day, take cognisance of the offence, record the facts the offence and the statement, if any, made by the offender and the offender (aJ in the case of a Syariah Subordinate Court, to a nne not exceeding $2,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both; (bJ in the case of the Syariah High Court and the Syariah Appeal nne not exceeding $10,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both: the court may\n\n(i) discharge the offende; or remit the punishment on his an apology to the satisfaction of the court;\n\n(ii) in lieu of taking cognisance of the offence, authorise a prosecution. of Judges. 28B. (1) The remuneration of the Syar'ie Judges shall be prescribed by the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan and such remuneration shall be charged upon the Consolidated Fund.\n\n(2) Remuneration for the purposes of subsection (l) shall include any which may become payable in respect of the services of the Syar'ie under any agreement entered into by Brunei Darussalam for the provision of such Syar'ie Judges and of their services. Protection of judicial and other officers. 28C. ( 1) A judicial officer shall not be liable to be sued in any court for any by him in the discharge of his judicial duty, whether or not within the limits of his juridiction, provided that at the time in good faith he believed himself to have jurisdiction to do that act.\n\n(2) No officer of a Syariah Court or other person charged with the duty of executing any writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other process of a Syariah Court shall be liable to be sued for the or attempting to execute such writ, summons, warrant, order, other mandatory process, or in respect of any damage caused to any property in effecting or attempting to effect execution, unless he in excess of the authority conferred upon him by such writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process in and he shall not be deemed to have acted knowingly in excess of his authority merely by reason of the existence of a dispute as to the ownership of any property seized under any writ or order or execution.\". of Chapter 77."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"text":{"en":"The Religious Council and Kadis Courts Act is amended by repealing sections 92 and 197. of S 12/2000."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"heading":{"en":"under Article 83{3))"},"text":{"en":"Section 134 of the Emergency (Islamic Family Law) Order, 1999 is repealed and the following new section substituted therefor Court."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2005-SEC-13-OF-THE-SYARIAH-COURTS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2005-A134","no":134,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 134."},"text":{"en":"Without prejudice to the provisions of any other written law, failure to with an order of the Court made under this Order shall be regarded as contempt of Court and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both.\". Made this 13th. day of Safar, 1426 Hjjriah corresponding to the 24th. day at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM AWANG MOHIDIN BIN HAJI DAUD, Pengarah Percetakan, di Jabatan Percetakan Kerajaan, Bandar Seri Begawan BB3510, Negara Brunei Darussalam."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"SEC 13 OF THE SYARIAH COURTS AMENDMENT ORDER 2005","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-17-2014-NOTIFICATION-OF-COMMENCEMENT"] = {"id":"BN-S-17-2014-NOTIFICATION-OF-COMMENCEMENT","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":"生效公告","en":"NOTIFICATION OF COMMENCEMENT","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 17/2014","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2014","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-17-2014-NOTIFICATION-OF-COMMENCEMENT.pdf》（1 页），本次切分 1 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-17-2014-NOTIFICATION-OF-COMMENCEMENT.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-17-2014-NOTIFICATION-OF-COMMENCEMENT-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"BRUNEI DARUSSALAM GOVERNMENT GAZETTE No. S 17\n\nSYARIAH PENAL CODE ORDER, 2013 (S 69/2013) Notification of commencement In exercise of the power conferred by section 1(1) and (2) of the Syariah Penal Code Order, 2013, the Minister of Religious Affairs, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, hereby appoints 1st Rejab 1435 Hijriah corresponding to the 1st May 2014 as the date of commencement for the provisions of that Order as set out in the Schedule hereto\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nPROVISIONS OF SYARIAH PENAL CODE ORDER, 2013\n\nPART I\n\nPART II\n\nPART III section 94 section 184 section 185 sections 189 to 205 sections 207 to 220 sections 228 to 253 section 254 (except references to sections 172, 194 and 195 of the Religious Council and Kadis Courts Act (Chapter 77)). Dated this 24th. day of Jamadilakhir, 1435 Hijriah corresponding to the 24th. day of April, 2014. PENGIRAN DATO SERI SETIA DR. HAJI MOHAMMAD\n\nBIN PENGIRAN HAJI ABDUL RAHMAN Minister of Religious Affairs, Brunei Darussalam. Dicetak oleh PENGIRAN HAJI ZAINAL ABIDIN BIN PENGIRAN SERI WIJAYA PENGIRAN HAJI AHMAD, Pengarah Percetakan, di Jabatan Percetakan Kerajaan, Bandar Seri Begawan BB3510, Negara Brunei Darussalam. Harga B$5.00 I"}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"NOTIFICATION OF COMMENCEMENT","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50"] = {"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":51,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"反人口贩运命令 2019 第 50 条","en":"ANTI TRAFFICKING IN PERSONS ORDER 2019 SEC. 50","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 17/2019","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2019","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC.-50.pdf》（26 页），本次切分 51 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC.-50.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"Citation and long title"},"text":{"en":"(1) This Order may be cited as the Anti-Trafficking in Persons Order, 2019.\n\n(2) The long title of this Order is \"An Order to criminalise people trafficking and for matters connected herewith or incidental thereto\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"Interpretation"},"text":{"en":"In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires - \"abduct\" means in relation to an individual, to compel by force, or induce by any deceitful means, the individual to go from any place; \"abuse of a position of vulnerability\" means taking advantage of the vulnerable position a person is placed in as a result of -\n\n(a) having entered the country illegally or\n\n(b) pregnancy or any physical or mental disease or disability of the person, including addiction to the use of any substance;\n\n(c) reduced capacity to form judgments by virtue of illness, infirmity or a physical or mental disability; \"abuse of power\" means any situation where a public officer uses his position or takes advantage of his position in order to commit an offence; \"child\" means a person who is under 18 years of age; \"coercion7' means use of force or threat thereof, and some forms of non-violent or psychological use of force or threat thereof, including but not\n\n(a) threats of harm or physical restraint of any person;\n\n(b) any scheme, plan or pattern intended to cause a person to believe that failure to perform an act would result in serious harm to or physical restraint against any person;\n\n(c) abuse or any threat linked to the legal status of a person; \"conveyance\" means any vehicle, vessel, ship, aircraft, or any other mode of transport whether by air, sea or land; \"debt bondage\" means a status or condition arising from -\n\n(a) the pledging by a debtor of the personal services of the debtor or an individual under the debtor's control, as security for a debt; and\n\n(b) the reasonable value of such services not being applied towards the discharge of the debt, or the length or nature of such services not being limited or defined, respectively; \"deception\" means any deception by words or by conduct as to -\n\n(a) the nature of work or services to be provided;\n\n(b) the conditions of work;\n\n(c) the extent to which the person will be free to leave his place of \"exploitation\" includes all forms of sexual exploitation (including sexual servitude and exploitation of another person's prostitution), forced labour or services, slavery or practices similar to slavery, servitude and the removal of \"forced labour or services\" means all work or service that is extracted from any person under the threat of any penalty and for which the person concerned has not offered himself voluntarily; \"forged travel or identity document\" means a travel or identity document that -\n\n(a) has been made, or altered in a material way, by a person other than a person or agency lawfully authorised to make or issue the travel or identity document on behalf of a country;\n\n(b) has been issued or obtained through misrepresentation, corruption or duress or in any other unlawful manner; or 6th. TULY. 2019\n\n(c) is being improperly used by a person other than the rightful holder; \"Fund\" means the Anti-Trafficking in Persons Fund established by section 44l1); \"harbour\" includes giving a person shelter, food, drink, money or clothes or means or the act of supplying conveyance, or assisting a person in any way to evade apprehension; \"master\" includes any person in command or having charge of any means of \"Minister\" means the Minister at the Prime Minister's Office; \"organised criminal group\" means a structured group of 3 or more persons existing for a period of time and acting in concert with the aim of committing one or more serious offence or offences established in accordance with this Order in order to obtain, directly or indirectly, a financial or other material \"owner\" includes any part-owner, charterer or consignee in possession thereof or any duly authorised agent of any such person; \"people trafficking\" means the recruitment, transportation, transfer, harbouring or receipt of a person for the purposes of exploitation as set out 5; \"premises\" includes -\n\n(a) a vehicle, ship, aircraft or hovercraft;\n\n(b) an installation which is maintained, or is intended to be established for underwater exploitation or exploration;\n\n(c) tent or other movable structure; \"public servant\" shall have the same meaning as a public servant under the Penal Code (Chapter 22); \"receiving country\" means any country or territory into which a trafficked person is brought or is arranged to be brought as part of an act of people \"serious offence\" means an offence under any other written law in Brunei Darussalam for which the maximum penalty is death, imprisonment for a term of not less than 6 months, fine of not less than $1,000 or more; \"servitude\", in relation to an individual, means any condition or obligation, not authorised by any written law, to work or to render services from which the individual cannot escape or which the individual is not free to change; \"sexual exploitation\" means involving the individual in prostitution, sexual servitude or the provision of any other form of sexual service, including the commission of any obscene or indecent act by the individual or the use of the individual in any audio or visual recording or representation of such act; \"shelter\" means any shelter declared as such under section 41; \"slavery\" means the status or condition of a person over whom control is exercised to the extent that the person is treated like property; \"trafficked person\" means any person who is the victim or object of an offence of people trafficking regardless of whether that person consented or not; \"transits\" means arriving and passing through Brunei Darussalam by any means of transport for the purpose of continuing journey by any means of transport to a place outside Brunei Darussalam; \"travel document\" includes an internationally recognised passport, a certificate of identity and any similar document, issued by an authority recognised by the receiving country."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"Application"},"text":{"en":"This Order applies, regardless of whether the conduct constituting the offence whether in whole or in part took place within or outside Brunei Darussalam, in the following circumstances -\n\n(a) if Brunei Darussalam is the receiving country or the people trafficking occurs in Brunei Darussalam;\n\n(b) if the receiving country is a foreign country but the people trafficking transits in Brunei Darussalam;\n\n(c) if the person who engages in people trafficking is a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or permanent resident; or\n\n(d) if the trafficked person is a citizen of Brunei Darussalam or a permanent resident."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"Authorised officers"},"text":{"en":"For the purposes of this Order, the following persons are authorised\n\n(a) an officer of the Royal Brunei Police Force;\n\n(b) an Immigration Officer appointed under section 3 of the Immigration Act (Chapter 17);\n\n(c) an officer of customs appointed under section 3(1) of the Customs Order, 2006 (S 3912006);\n\n(d) an authorised officer appointed under section 3(1) of the Employment Order, 2009 (S 3712009); or\n\n(e) such person or class of persons appointed by the Minister and designated by notification published in the Gazette.\n\nPART I1"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"People trafficking"},"text":{"en":"(1) Any person who recruits, transports, transfers, harbours or receives any person or persons for the purpose of exploitation by one or more of the following\n\n(a) abduction;\n\n(b) abuse of power or of a position of vulnerability;\n\n(c) deception;\n\n(d) fraud;\n\n(e) the giving or receiving of payments or benefits to achieve the consent of a person having control over another person; (fl threat;\n\n(g) use of force or other forms of coercion, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 and not less than $10,000 in respect of each trafficked person, imprisonment for a term of not less than 4 years but not exceeding 30 years and whipping.\n\n(2) Where the recruitment, transportation, transfer, harbouring or receipt under subsection (1) for the purpose of exploitation is in respect of a child, it shall be considered trafficking in persons even if it does not involve any of the means referred to subsection (11, the person is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 and not less than $10,000 in respect of each trafficked child, imprisonment for a term of not less than 4 years but not exceeding 30 years and whipping with not less than 5 strokes.\n\n(3) Where any of the following aggravating circumstances are present during the commission of an offence under this section -\n\n(a) the offence involves serious injury or death of the trafficked person or another person, including death as a result of suicide;\n\n(b) the offence involves a trafficked person who is particularly vulnerable such as a person who is unable to fully take care of or protect himself because of a physical or mental disability or condition;\n\n(c) the offence exposed the trafficked person to a life-threatening illness, including Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) and Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome (AIDS);\n\n(d) the offence involves more than one trafficked person;\n\n(e) the offence was committed as part of the activity of an organised (fl the offender has been previously convicted for an offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder;\n\n(g) the offence was committed by a public servant in the performance of his public duties;\n\n(h) the offender used drugs, weapons or medication in the commission\n\n(i) the offender used a child as an accomplice or participant in the\n\n(j) the offender used or threatened to use any form of violence against the trafficked person or his family;\n\n(h) the offender confiscated, destroyed or attempted to destroy the travel or identity documents of the trafficked person, the offender is liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 and not less than $10,000 for each trafficked person, imprisonment for a term of not less than 4 years but not exceeding 30 years and whipping with not less than 5 strokes."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"heading":{"en":"Sexual trafficking"},"text":{"en":"Any person who, with the intention of inducing another person to enter into an engagement to provide sexual services, deceives that other person about -\n\n(a) the fact that the engagement will involve the provision of sexual\n\n(b) the nature of sexual services to be provided;\n\n(c) the extent to which the person will be free to cease providing sexual\n\n(d) if there is or will be a debt owed or claimed to be owed by the person in connection with the engagement, the quantum, or the existence, of the debt owed or claimed to be owed;\n\n(e) the fact that the engagement will involve debt bondage or the confiscation of the person's travel documents, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000, imprisonment for a term of not less than 4 years but not exceeding 30 years and whipping with not less than 5 strokes. of trafficked person"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"heading":{"en":"Exploitation of trafficked person"},"text":{"en":"Any person who -\n\n(a) engages in; or\n\n(b) profits from, the exploitation of a trafficked person is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000, imprisonment for a term of not less than 4 years but not exceeding 30 years and whipping."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"heading":{"en":"Trafficked person in transit"},"text":{"en":"Any person who brings in transit a trafficked person through Brunei Darussalam by land, sea or air, or otherwise arranges or facilitates such act is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000, imprisonment for a term of not less than 4 years but not exceeding 30 years and whipping."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"heading":{"en":"Consent of trafficked person irrelevant"},"text":{"en":"For the purposes of sections 5jl), 5(2), 5(3), 6, 7 and 8, it shall not be a defence if the trafficked person has consented to people trafficking."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"heading":{"en":"Forgery of travel or identity document"},"text":{"en":"Any person who -\n\n(a) makes;\n\n(b) obtains;\n\n(c) gives;\n\n(d) sells; or\n\n(e) possesses, a forged travel or identity document for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence of people trafficking is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or both."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"heading":{"en":"Obligation of owner etc. of conveyance"},"text":{"en":"(1) Any person being the owner, operator or master of any conveyance that engages in the conveyance of goods or people for commercial gain shall ensure that every person travelling on board is in possession of travel documents for the lawful entry of that person into the receiving country or transit country, and if not, shall refuse to convey such person.\n\n(2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or both.\n\n(3) In any proceedings for an offence under this section, it shall be a defence for such owner, operator or master to prove that -\n\n(a) he has reasonable grounds to believe that the travel documents of the person referred to in subsection (1) are travel documents required for lawful entry of that person into the receiving country or transit country;\n\n(b) the person referred to in subsection (1) possessed travel documents required for lawful entry to the receiving country or transit country when that person boarded, or last boarded, the conveyance to travel to the receiving country or transit country; or\n\n(c) the entry of the person referred to in subsection (1) into the receiving or transit country occurred only because of illness or injury to that person, stress of weather or any other circumstances beyond the control of such owner, operator or master.\n\n(4) Any person convicted of an offence under this section is liable to pay the costs of the trafficked person's removal from the receiving country or transit\n\n(5) Where there is no prosecution or conviction under this section, the owner, operator or master of the conveyance used shall be jointly and severally liable for all expenses incurred by the Government in respect of the maintenance of the trafficked person and his removal from Brunei Darussalam and such expenses shall be recoverable as a debt due to the Government.\n\n(6) In this section, \"transit country\" means the country from which, or into or through which, a trafficked person, is brought or travels through by air, land or sea or temporarily remains in as part of an act of people trafficking."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"heading":{"en":"Recruitment of persons"},"text":{"en":"Any person who knowingly recruits, or agrees to recruit another person to participate in the commission of an offence of people trafficking is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"heading":{"en":"Attempts, abetment and conspiracy"},"text":{"en":"(1) Whoever attempts to commit any offence punishable under this Order or any regulations made thereunder, or abets the commission of such offence, shall be punished with the punishment provided for such offence.\n\n(2) Any person who conspires with another person to commit an offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder is guilty of the offence of conspiracy to commit that offence and may be punished as if the offence to which the conspiracy relates had been committed. Offences by bodies corporate"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"heading":{"en":"6th. JULY, 2019"},"text":{"en":"Where an offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder has been committed by a company, firm, society or other body of persons, any person who at the time of the commission of the offence was a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer or a partner of the company, firm, society or other body of persons or has purporting to act in such capacity is deemed to be guilty of that offence unless he proves that the offence was committed without his consent or connivance and that he exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he ought to have exercised, having regard to the nature of his functions in that capacity and to all the circumstances. Facilitating the commission of people trafficking"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"text":{"en":"Any person being the owner, occupier, lessee or person in charge of -\n\n(a) any premises, room or place, knowingly permits a meeting to be held in that premises, room or place; or\n\n(b) any equipment or facility that allows for recording, conferencing or meetings by means of technology, knowingly permits that equipment or facility to be used, for the purpose of committing an offence against this Order is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or both. Providing financial services or facilities for people trafficking"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"text":{"en":"(1) Any person who, directly or indirectly, provides or makes available financial services or facilities -\n\n(a) intending that the services or facilities will be used, or knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe that the services or facilities will be used, in whole or in part, for the purpose of committing or facilitating the commission of an offence of people trafficking, or for the purpose of benefiting any person who is committing or facilitating the commission of an offence of people trafficking; or\n\n(b) knowingly or having reasonable grounds to believe that, in whole or in any part, the services or facilities will be used by or will benefit any person involved in an offence of people trafficking, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or both. 12) For the purposes of subsection ( I ) , \"financial services or facilities\" include the services or facilities offered by lawyers or accountants acting as nominees or agents for their clients. Powers of arrest and investigation"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"[I] An authorised officer may arrest without warrant any person who he reasonably believes has committed an offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder.\n\n(2) When any person is arrested by an authorised officer, such officer shall comply with the provisions of section 33 of the Criminal Procedure Code (Chapter 71.\n\n(3) In any case relating to the commission of any offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder, an authorised officer shall have the same powers of investigation of a police officer under Chapter XI11 of the Criminal Procedure Code (Chapter 7)."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"(1) An authorised officer may without a warrant -\n\n(a) enter and search any premises; and\n\n(b) stop and search any conveyance and person, whether in a public if he has reason to believe that any evidence of the commission of an offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder is likely to be found on such premises or person or in such conveyance and may seize any evidence so\n\n(2) No woman shall be searched under this section except by a woman. Access to computerised data"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"(1) Any authorised officer conducting a search under this Order shall be given access to computerised data whether stored in a computer or otherwise.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (I), the authorised officer shall be provided with the necessary password, encryption code, decryption code, software or hardware or any other means required for his access to enable comprehension of the computerised data.\n\n(3) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for each day during which the offence continues after\n\n(4) In this section, \"computer\" means any device for storing and processing information, and any reference to information being derived from other information is a reference to its being derived therefrom by calculation, comparison or any other process. to examine persons"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"(1) An authorised officer may, by notice in writing, require any person whom he believes to be acquainted with the facts and circumstances of the case to -\n\n(a) attend before him for examination;\n\n(b) produce before him any movable property, record, report or\n\n(c) furnish him a statement in writing setting out such information as he may require.\n\n(2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both, and in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $2,000 for each day during which the offence continues after Power to intercept telecommunications"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"(1) Notwithstanding the provisions of any other written law, if the Public Prosecutor considers that it is likely to contain any information which is relevant for the purpose of any investigation into an offence against this Order, he may, on the application of an authorised officer, authorise the officer -\n\n(a) to intercept, detain and open any postal article in the course of transmission by post;\n\n(b) to intercept any message transmitted or received by any telecommunication; or\n\n(c) to intercept, listen to and record any conversation by any telecommunication, and listen to the recording of conversation.\n\n(2) When any person is charged with an offence against this Order, any information obtained by an authorised officer under subsection ( I ) , whether before or after such person is charged, shall be admissible at his trial in evidence.\n\n(3) An authorisation by the Public Prosecutor under subsection [I) may be given either orally or in writing; but if an oral authorisation is given, the Public Prosecutor shall, as soon as practicable, reduce the authorisation into writing.\n\n(4) A certificate by the Public Prosecutor stating that the action taken by the authorised officer under subsection (I.) had been authorised by him under that subsection shall be conclusive evidence that it had been so authorised, and such certificate shall be admissible in evidence without proof of signature thereof.\n\n(5) No person shall be under any duty, obligation or liability, or be in any manner compelled, to disclose in any proceedings the procedure, method, manner or means, or any matter related thereto, of any thing done under (].](a), (b) or (c).\n\n(6) In this section - \"postal article\" has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Post Office \"Public Prosecutor\" means the Public Prosecutor personally; \"telecommunication\" has the same meaning as in section 2 of the Telecommunications Order, 2001 (S 381200 I. 1. Provision of telecommunication records"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"Any telecommunications authority established in Brunei Darussalam shall provide telecommunication records of a person under investigation for committing or attempting to commit an offence against this Order if required to do so by any authorised officer. False statements, information etc."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"Any person who, being required to make any statement or furnish any information or document under this Order -\n\n(a) makes any statement or furnishes any information or document which is false or misleading in a material particular; and\n\n(b) knows or ought reasonably to know that, or is reckless as to whether, it is false or misleading in a material particular, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or both."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"Any person who assaults, obstructs, impedes, hinders, interferes or fails to comply with any lawful demand of an authorised officer in the performance of his functions under this Order is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or both. Cost of holding conveyance, movable property etc. seized"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"Where any conveyance, movable property, record, report, document or human organ seized under this Order is held in the custody of the authorised officer pending completion of any proceedings in respect of an offence against this Order, the cost of holding such conveyance, movable property, record, report or document or human organ in custody shall, in the event of any person being found guilty of an offence, be a civil debt due to the Government by such person and shall be recoverable accordingly. Release of conveyance, movable property etc. under bond"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26."},"chapter":{"en":"PART 111"},"text":{"en":"(1) Where any conveyance, movable property, record, report or document has been seized under this Order, an authorised officer may temporarily return such conveyance, movable property, record, report or document to the owner on security or bond being furnished to the satisfaction of such authorised officer and subject to such conditions as such authorised officer may impose, that the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document shall be surrendered to him on demand.\n\n(2) Any person who fails to -\n\n(a) surrender on demand to an authorised officer the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document temporarily returned to him under subsection (1); or\n\n(b) comply with or contravenes any of the conditions imposed under (11, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or both, and any security or bond being furnished shall be forfeited.\n\nIN COURT Offences to be non-bailable and seizable"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"Every offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder is non-bailable and seizable for the purposes of the law relating to criminal Consent of Public Prosecutor"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"No prosecution for any offence against this Order shall be instituted except with the consent in writing of the Public Prosecutor. Evidence through video link"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"Evidence of a trafficked person shall be heard through a video link or behind a screen out of the view of the accused. Evidence of trafficked child"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"The inquiry into and trial where the trafficked person is a child shall be conducted in camera. Taking of evidence before trial"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"(1) Subject to subsection (2), where an application is made by the Public Prosecutor or the accused to a court for the evidence of a witness to be taken at any time before the date on which a criminal matter is fixed for trial, the court shall take the evidence of the witness appearing before it.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) can only be made if it is shown with respect to the witness that it is not reasonably practicable to secure his attendance at the time fixed for the trial.\n\n(3) The proceedings under this section must be conducted in the presence of the accused and co-accused, if any.\n\n(4) The witness called by a party to give evidence in the proceedings under this section may be cross-examined by any other party to the proceedings, after which the witness may be re-examined by the party calling him to give\n\n(5) Any statement of a witness taken in proceedings under this section may be given in evidence in any trial under this Order (whether or not by the same judge hearing the proceedings) although the person is not called as a witness. Admissibility of statements"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"Notwithstanding any written law to the contrary, for the purposes of any proceedings under this Order -\n\n(a) any statement made by any person to an authorised officer in the course of an investigation under this Order; and\n\n(b) any document, or copy of any document, seized from any person by an authorised officer in exercise of his powers under this Order, shall be admissible in evidence in any proceedings under this Order before any court, where the person who made the statement or the document or the copy of the document -\n\n(i) is dead;\n\n(ii) cannot be traced or found;\n\n(iii) has become incapable of giving evidence; or (iv] whose attendance cannot be procured without an amount of delay or expense which appears to the court unreasonable. Past sexual behaviour irrelevant"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"In a prosecution for trafficking in persons, evidence of a trafficked person's past sexual behaviour is irrelevant and inadmissible for the purpose of proving that the trafficked person engaged in other sexual behaviour or to prove the trafficked person's sexual predisposition. Movement or conveyance of trafficked person irrelevant"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"In a prosecution for any offence against this Order, the prosecution need not prove the movement or conveyance of the trafficked person but that the trafficked person was subject to exploitation."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Penalties to be cumulative"},"text":{"en":"For the avoidance of any doubt, where more than one penalty is prescribed for an offence against this Order, the use of the word \"and\" shall signify that the penalties shall be inflicted cumulatively."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Application of fines"},"text":{"en":"In respect of the fines imposed for the contravention of sections 5(1), 5(2), 5(3], 6, 7 and 8 or for an abetment of or conspiracy or attempt to commit such offences, the court may upon the application of the Public Prosecutor and, if it thinks fit, direct that the whole or any part of such fine be paid as compensation to the trafficked person. Forfeiture of conveyance, movable property etc."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"(1) All conveyance, movable property, record, report, document or any human organ seized in the exercise of any power conferred under this Order are liable to forfeiture.\n\n(2) The court trying any person accused of an offence under this Order may at the conclusion of the trial, whether he is convicted or not, order that the conveyance, movable property, record, report, document or any human organ seized from that person be forfeited.\n\n(3) Where there is no prosecution with regard to any offence under this\n\n(a) in the case of any human organ seized, it shall be deemed to be\n\n(b) in the case of the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document seized, the authorised officer shall serve a notice in writing to the last known address of the person from whom the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document was seized.\n\n(4) The notice in subsection (3)(b) shall specify that if there is no prosecution in respect of such conveyance, movable property, record, report or document and that such conveyance, movable property, record, report or document shall be forfeited at the expiration of one calendar month from the date of service of the notice unless a claim is made by the person from whom the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document was seized.\n\n(5) Upon receipt of the notice issued under subsection (3)(b), any person asserting that he is the owner of any conveyance, movable property, record, report or document seized under this Order which is not liable to forfeiture may, personally or by his agent authorised in writing by him, give written notice to the authorised officer in whose possession the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document is held.\n\n(6) Upon receipt of a notice under subsection (51, the authorised officer who made the seizure shall refer the matter to the court for its determination.\n\n(7) The court to which the matter is referred shall issue a summons requiring the person asserting that he is the owner of the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document and the person from whom it was seized to appear before the court, and upon their appearance or default to appear, due service of the summons being proved, the court shall proceed to the examination of the matter, and on proof that such conveyance, movable property, record, report or document was the subject matter of or was used in the commission of an offence under this Order, shall order the conveyance, movable property, record, report or document to be forfeited or may, in the absence of such proof, order the release of such conveyance, movable property, record, report or document to the person entitled to it.\n\n(8) Any conveyance, movable property, record, report, document or any human organ forfeited or deemed to be forfeited shall be disposed of in any manner as the authorised officer deems fit."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Protection of identity of trafficked persons"},"text":{"en":"(1) No person shall publish or cause to be published any material which -\n\n(a) reveals the name or address; or\n\n(b) includes any particulars which may lead to the identification, of any trafficked person in respect of whom the offence is alleged to have been\n\n(2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine of $10,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (I.], \"material\" includes a photograph."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A39","no":39,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 39."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Agent provocateur"},"text":{"en":"(1) Notwithstanding any written law to the contrary, in any proceedings against any person for an offence against this Order, no agent provocateur, whether he is an authorised officer or not, shall be presumed to be unworthy of credit by reason only of his having attempted to commit or to abet, or having abetted or having been engaged in a criminal conspiracy to commit, such offence if the main purpose of such attempt, abetment or engagement was to secure evidence against such person.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding any written law to the contrary, a conviction for any offence against this Order solely on the uncorroborated evidence of any agent shall not be illegal and no such conviction shall be set aside merely because the court which tried the case has failed to refer in the grounds of its judgment to the need to warn itself against the danger of convicting on such Protection of informants"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A40","no":40,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 40."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"CARE AND PROTECTION OF TRAFFICKED PERSONS"},"text":{"en":"(1) Except as hereinafter provided, no complaint as to an offence or any proceedings under this Order shall be admitted in evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings whatsoever, and no witness shall be obliged or permitted to disclose the name or address of any informer or state any matter which might lead to his discovery.\n\n(2) If any books, documents or papers which are in evidence or liable to inspection in any civil or criminal proceedings whatsoever contain any entry in which any informer is named or described or which might lead to his discovery, the court before which the proceeding is had shall cause all such passage to be concealed from view or to be obliterated so far as is necessary to protect the informer from discovery."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A41","no":41,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 41."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Shelter"},"text":{"en":"The Minister may, by notification published in the Gazette, declare any place to be a shelter for the purposes of this Order."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A42","no":42,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 42."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Removing or helping trafficked person to escape from shelter"},"text":{"en":"(1) If a trafficked person is placed in a shelter, any person who -\n\n(a) removes the trafficked person from such shelter without lawful\n\n(b) knowingly assists or induces, directly or indirectly, a trafficked person to escape from such shelter; or\n\n(c) knowingly harbours, conceals, or prevents from returning to such shelter a trafficked person who has escaped, or knowingly assists in so doing, is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or both.\n\n(2) If any trafficked person who is placed in a shelter is removed without lawful authority, or escapes, from such shelter, he may be retaken by any authorised officer and immediately returned to such shelter. Assistance to trafficked persons"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A43","no":43,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 43."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"ANTI-TRAFFICKING IN PERSONS FUND"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Director may provide to a trafficked person such assistance as the Director considers appropriate in the particular circumstances of the case,\n\n(a) shelter;\n\n(b) temporary accommodation;\n\n(c) counselling services;\n\n(d) medical and psychological assistance; and\n\n(e) employment, educational and training opportunities.\n\n(2) The Minister may -\n\n(a) appoint any public officer; or\n\n(b) authorise in writing any other person, to perform the Director's function under subsection (I), subject to such conditions and limitations as the Director may specify.\n\n(3) For the avoidance of doubt, any appointment or authorisation under subsection (2) does not restrict or prevent the Director from exercising the functions under subsection (1).\n\n(4) Any person appointed or authorised under subsection (2) is deemed to be a public servant within the meaning of the Penal Code (Chapter 22).\n\n(5) In this section, \"Director\" means the Director of the Department of Community Development.\n\nPART V1"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A44","no":44,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 44."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Anti-Trafficking in Persons Fund"},"text":{"en":"(1) There is hereby established a fund called the Anti-Trafficking in Persons Fund.\n\n(2) The Fund shall be administered and managed by the Permanent"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A45","no":45,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 45."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Money to be paid into Fund"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Minister, may authorise the payment into the Fund of such sum or sums as may be necessary to set up or maintain it, and any such payments shall be charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund.\n\n(2) The Fund shall consist of -\n\n(a) all amounts contributed by the Government towards the establishment or maintenance of the Fund from the Consolidated Fund or any other sources;\n\n(b) all sums recovered under or in satisfaction of a judgment of any court under this Order;\n\n(c) subject to section 36, all fines imposed by any court under this\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Order, monies paid into the Fund do not form part of the Consolidated Fund. Fund"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A46","no":46,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 46."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Purposes of Fund"},"text":{"en":"(1) Subject to subsection (2), monies in the Fund shall be applied for the following purposes -\n\n(a) compensation to trafficked persons;\n\n(b) financing the cost of repatriation of trafficked persons;\n\n(c) to enable the appropriate law enforcement agencies to continue their fight against people trafficking; (dl the promotion of information and education of the public in preventing, suppressing or otherwise of people trafficking;\n\n(e) rewards to any person in preventing or suppressing people\n\n(f) such other purposes as the Minister may consider necessary or expedient for giving effect to and carrying out the provisions of this Order.\n\n(2) The Permanent Secretary shall consult the Attorney General before applying the Fund for any of the purposes set out in subsection (1).\n\n(3) Monies paid into the Fund, while not being applied for any of the purposes set out in subsection [l), shall be placed in the name of the Fund, in a current or deposit account, with one or more banks selected by the Permanent Secretary, and any interest earned on such monies while held in any such account shall be credited to such account.\n\n(4) The accounts of the Fund shall be audited at least once annually by the Auditor General and the duly audited accounts shall be presented to the Minister of Finance.\n\n(5) In this section and section 44(2), \"Permanent Secretary\" means the Permanent Secretary to the Office of the Prime Minister."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A47","no":47,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 47."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Immunity from criminal prosecution"},"text":{"en":"A trafficked person shall not be liable to criminal prosecution in respect of -\n\n(a) his illegal entry into Brunei Darussalam;\n\n(b) his period of unlawful residence in Brunei Darussalam; or\n\n(c) his procurement or possession of any fraudulent travel or identity document which he obtained, or with which he was supplied, for the purpose of entering Brunei Darussalam, where such acts are the direct consequence of an offence of people trafficking that is alleged to have been committed or was committed."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A48","no":48,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 48."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Offender deemed to be prohibited immigrant"},"text":{"en":"A person, not being a citizen of Brunei Darussalam, convicted for any offence against this Order or any regulations made thereunder is deemed to be a prohibited immigrant under section 8 of the Immigration Act (Chapter 17)."}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A49","no":49,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 49."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Regulations"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, make regulations which are necessary or expedient for giving effect to and carrying out the provisions of this Order, including any other thing for the due administration thereof.\n\n(2) Such regulations may include such incidental, consequential and supplementary provisions as the Minister considers necessary or expedient.\n\nS 8212004"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A50","no":50,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 50."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"Repeal of S 8212004"},"text":{"en":"Subject to section 51, the Trafficking and Smuggling of Persons Order, 2004 is hereby repealed. Transitional and savings provision"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2019-ANTI-TRAFFICKING-IN-PERSONS-ORDER-2019-SEC-50-A51","no":51,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 51."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"heading":{"en":"CONSTITUTION OF BRUNEI DARUSSALAM"},"text":{"en":"(1) On the date of commencement of this Order, the Trafficking and Smuggling of Persons Fund established by section 19 of the repealed Trafficking and Smuggling of Persons Order, 2004 (S 8212004) shall be known as the Anti-Trafficking in Persons Fund established under section 44 and all monies which immediately before the commencement of this Order was vested in the Trafficking and Smuggling of Persons Fund shall be transferred to and shall vest in the Anti-Trafficking in Persons Fund without further assurance.\n\n(2) Anything done or made under the repealed 'Ikafficking and Smuggling of Persons Order, 2004 and in force immediately before the date of commencement of this Order and so far as it is not inconsistent with this Order shall continue to be in force as if done under this Order, until it is amended, or repealed under this Order.\n\n(3) The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, by order published in the Gazette, make such other transitional and savings provisions as he may consider necessary and expedient. Made this 3rd. day of Zulkaedah, 1440 Hijriah corresponding to the 6th. day of July, 2019 at our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN, BRUNEI DARUSSALAM."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"ANTI TRAFFICKING IN PERSONS ORDER 2019 SEC. 50","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-17-2021-E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMEND-6D008D"] = {"id":"BN-S-17-2021-E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMEND-6D008D","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"文莱达鲁萨兰国金融管理局修正命令 2021","en":"AUTORITI MONETARI BRUNEI DARUSSALAM AMENDMENT ORDER 2021","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 17/2021","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2021","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-17_2021_E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2021.pdf》（3 页），本次切分 4 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-17_2021_E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2021.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-17-2021-E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMEND-6D008D-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of section 1 of S 103/2010"},"text":{"en":"Section 1 of the Autoriti Monetari Brunei Darussalam Order, 2010, in this to as the principal Order, is amended - fa} in subsection {1), by deleting \"Autoriti Monetari Brunei by substituting \"Brunei Darussalam Central Bank\" fbi {2), by deleting \"Autoriti Monetari Brunei to act as the central bank of Brunei Darussalam,\" from the and third lines and by substituting \"\"Brunei Darussalam Central of section 2 3-Section 2 of the principal Order is amended - fa} in the definition of \"\"Authority\"\", by deleting \"\"Autoriti Monetari Brunei Darussalam\" and by substituting '\"Brunei Darussalam Central Bank\" fbi in the definition of '\"Minister\", by inserting '\"and Economy'\" immediately after '\"Finance\"_ of section 3"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2021-E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMEND-6D008D-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of section 3"},"text":{"en":"Section 3 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection {1). by deleting known as the Autoriti Monetari Brunei Darussalam'\" and by \"\"the Brunei Darussalam Central Bank\" therefor. of section 56"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2021-E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMEND-6D008D-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of section 56"},"text":{"en":"Section 56 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (lOj, by deleting \"Autoriti Monetari Brunei Darussalam\"' from the last two lines and by substituting '\"Brunei Darussalam Central Bank\" therefor. and transitional provisions"}},{"id":"BN-S-17-2021-E-AUTORITI-MONETARI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-AMEND-6D008D-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"heading":{"en":"BRUNEI DARUSSALAM GOVERNMENT GAZETTE"},"text":{"en":"111 Any right, benefit, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or or any act or thing done or required to be done, shall not be affected by this Order and shall continue to remain valid and have effect as if this Order had not been enacted. (21 This Order shall not affect any inquiry, investigation or proceedings or pending before the commencement of this Order and every such inquiry, investigation or proceedings may be continued and dealt with as if this had not been enacted. (3J In so far as it is necessary for preserving the effect of any written law or document, any reference in such written law or document to the Autoriti Monetari Brunei Darussalam shall, as from the commencement of this Order, be construed as a reference to the Brunei Darussalam Central Bank. Made this 15th. day of Zulkaedah, 1442 Hijriah corresponding to the 26th. day of June, 2021.\n\nHIS MAJESTY THE SULTAN AND YANG DJ.PERTUAN, DARUSSALAM."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"AUTORITI MONETARI BRUNEI DARUSSALAM AMENDMENT ORDER 2021","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-18-1988-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-BRIGADE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1988"] = {"id":"BN-S-18-1988-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-BRIGADE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1988","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"紧急消防队法修正命令 1988","en":"EMERGENCY FIRE BRIGADE ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 1988","orig":null},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"S 18/1988","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"1988","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-18_1988_E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-BRIGADE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1988.pdf》（1 页），本次切分 3 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-18_1988_E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-BRIGADE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1988.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-18-1988-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-BRIGADE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1988-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Emergency (Fire Brigade AdJ Short title and (Amendment). Order 1988 and shall be deemed to have come into commenceforce on the 9th November 1987."}},{"id":"BN-S-18-1988-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-BRIGADE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1988-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"The Fire Brigade Act (hereinafter referred to as \"the Act\") Amendment of shall with effect from the commencement of this Order be cited as the the title of the \"Fire Service Act\" and wherever a reference is made in any written Act. law to the \"Fire Brigade Act\" it shall be construed as a reference to the \"Fire Service Act\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-18-1988-E-EMERGENCY-FIRE-BRIGADE-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1988-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"The Act is amended by deleting the words specified in the First Column of the Schedule to this Order wherever the said words appear in the Act and substituting therefor the words specified in the Second Column opposite thereto -\n\nSCHEDULE First Column Second Column Fire Brigade Fire Service Controller Director Deputy Controller Deputy Director Divisional Officer Superintendent Fire Brigade General Orders Fire Service General Orders Made this 2nd day of June 1988, at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM"}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"EMERGENCY FIRE BRIGADE ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 1988","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-18-2010-E-NOTIFICATION-UNDER-SECTION-11"] = {"id":"BN-S-18-2010-E-NOTIFICATION-UNDER-SECTION-11","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":"依第 11 条作出的公告","en":"NOTIFICATION UNDER SECTION 11","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 18/2010","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2010","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-18_2010_E-NOTIFICATION-UNDER-SECTION-11.pdf》（1 页），本次切分 1 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-18_2010_E-NOTIFICATION-UNDER-SECTION-11.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-18-2010-E-NOTIFICATION-UNDER-SECTION-11-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"BRUNEI DARUSSALAM GOVERNMENT GAZETTE No. S 18\n\nARBITRATION ORDER, 2009 (S 34/09) NOTIFICATION UNDER SECTION 1(1) In exercise of the power conferred by section 1[1), the Attorney General, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di~Pertuan, hereby appoints the day of the signing of this notification as the day of commencement of the Arbitration Order, 2009. Date this 9th. day of Rabiulawal, 1431 Hijriah corresponding to the 23rd. day of February, 2010.\n\nDATIN PADUKA HAJAH HAYATI BINTI\n\nPEHIN ORANG KAYA SHAHBANDAR DATO SERI PADUKA HAJI MOHD. SALLEH Attorney General, Brunei Darussalam. Dicetak oleh PENGIRAN HAJI ZAINAL ABIDIN BIN PENGIRAN SERI WIJAYA PENGIRAN HAJI AHMAD, Pemangku Pengarah Percetakan, di Jabatan Percetakan Kerajaan, Bandar Seri Begawan BB3510, Negara Brunei Darussalam. Harga B$5.00"}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"NOTIFICATION UNDER SECTION 11","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019"] = {"id":"BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"2019 年度 APEQS 修正命令","en":"APEQS AMENDMENT ORDER 2019","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 18/2019","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2019","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-18_2019_E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019.pdf》（6 页），本次切分 6 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-18_2019_E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"Citation and commencement"},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Architects, Professional Engineers and Quantity Surveyors (Amendment) Order, 2019 and shall be deemed to have commenced on the same date as the Architects, Professional Engineers and Quantity Surveyors Order, 20 1 1 (S 33/20 1 1)."}},{"id":"BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of section 1 of S 331201 1"},"text":{"en":"Section 1 of the Architects, Professional Engineers and Quantity Surveyors Order, 201 1, in this Order referred to as the principal Order, is amended, in\n\n(a) by deleting \"and quantity surveyors\" from the third line and by \", quantity surveyors and building draughtsmen\" therefor;\n\n(b) by deleting \"and quantity surveyors\" from the fourth and fifth lines and by substituting \", quantity surveyors and building draughtsmen\""}},{"id":"BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of section 4"},"text":{"en":"Section 4 of the principal Order is amended, in subsection (5), by deleting \"3 years\" and by substituting \"not more than 3 years\" therefor."}},{"id":"BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of section 6"},"text":{"en":"Section 6 of the principal Order is amended, in paragraph (e), by inserting \", or charged by building draughtsmen for services,\" immediately after \"services\". Insertion of new Part VII"}},{"id":"BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"CONSTITUTION OF BRUNEI DARUSSALAM"},"text":{"en":"The principal Order is amended by inserting the following new Part immediately after section 50 - 8th. JULY, 2019 , I\n\nSPECIAL PROVISIONS RELATING TO BUILDING DRAUGHTSMEN Interpretation for this Part I 50A. In this Part - I \"certificate of registration\" means the certificate of registration issued under I \"register\" means the register of building draughtsmen referred to in section 50C(1); I \"registered building draughtsman\" means a building draughtsman who has been issued with a certificate of registration under this Part. Illegal practice of unregistered building draughtsmen , 50B. (I] No person shall, unless he is a registered building draughtsman -\n\n(a) practice or carry on business as a building draughtsman;\n\n(b) use verbally or otherwise -\n\n(i) the word \"building draughtsman\" or any other derivatives in 1 connection with his business designation;\n\n(ii) any word, name or designation that might lead to the belief that he is a registered building draughtsman;\n\n(c) use or display any sign, board, card or other device representing or implying that he is a registered building draughtsman;\n\n(d) advertise or hold himself out or conduct himself in any way or by 1 any means as a person who is authorised to supply services; or I\n\n(e) be entitled to recover in any court any charge, fee or remuneration for any services rendered.\n\n(2) Any person who contravenes subsection (lj is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction - I\n\n(a) in respect of a first offence, to a fine not exceeding $10,000; and. '\n\n(b) in respect of a second or subsequent offence, to a fine not exceeding $20,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or both. Register of building draughtsmen 50C. (1) For the purposes of this Part, the Board shall keep and maintain at its office a register of building draughtsmen in which shall be entered all the names of building draughtsmen registered under this Part, the business addresses, the qualifications by virtue of which they are so registered and such other particulars as the Board may determine.\n\n(2) The Registrar shall -\n\n(a) as soon as practicable after 1st January each year, prepare and Gazette a list containing the names, qualifications and addresses of all registered building draughtsmen;\n\n(b) publish in the Gazette the names, qualifications and addresses of registered building draughtsmen removed from or reinstated into the register of building draughtsmen. Application of registration 50D. (1) A building draughtsman who has been registered with, and been issued with a certificate of registration by, the Board before 1st February 2016, may apply for registration under this Part and continue to practice as a registered building draughtsman.\n\n(2) The application for registration shall be made to the Board in such form and manner as the Board may determine. Certificate of registration 50E. ( I The Registrar shall, on payment of a fee of $150, issue to any applicant whose application has been approved by the Board, a certificate of registration.\n\n(2) The certificate of registration shall, subject to this Part and such other conditions as the Board may determine, expire on the 31st December of the year in which it is issued and shall thereafter be renewable upon payment of a fee of $100. of change of address of registered building draughtsmen 50F. Any change to the business address shall be notified by the registered building draughtsman to the Registrar within 2 weeks of such change. Restrictions on registered building draughtsmen 50G. (1) A registered building draughtsman shall, notwithstanding the provisions of any written law to the contrary, be entitled to submit plans of buildings to the building authority in accordance with the restrictions specified in\n\n(4) or such other restrictions as the Board thinks fit to impose.\n\n(2) No person who is employed by a body corporate, partnership, limited liability partnership, building contractor, manufacturer or firm shall be entitled td be registered under this Part.\n\n(3) No registered building draughtsman shall practise under the name of a body corporate, partnership and limited liability partnership.\n\n(4) Subject to subsection ( I ) , the registered building draughtsman shall be entitled to submit to a building authority for approval of any plans of buildings for residence not exceeding two-storeys in height provided that the total built-up floor area does not exceed 300 square metres in any one or series of project in the same development by the same client. Disciplinary proceedings and removal from register 50H. (1) The Board may appoint an Investigation Committee comprising -\n\n(a) a chairman who is a member of the Board;\n\n(b) a registered building draughtsman; and\n\n(c) an allied professional or a layman, to investigate into any misconduct or complaint made against a registered building draughtsman.\n\n(2) Sections 36, 37, 41, 42, 44 to 50 shall, with the necessary modifications, apply to the disciplinary proceedings of a registered building\n\n(3) For the purposes of applying sections 36, 37, 41, 42, 44 to 50, a reference in those provisions to registered architect, registered professional engineer or registered quantity surveyor shall be treated as a reference to a registered building draughtsman.\n\n(4) For the purposes of applying section 42(2), a Disciplinary Committee for any complaint against a registered building draughtsman shall comprise -\n\n(a) a registered architect who is a member of the Board; and\n\n(b) two registered building draughtsmen of at least 5 years standing.\n\n(5) For the purposes of applying section 47(2)/b), a reference to a period of 2 years shall be treated as a reference to such period as the Board Reinstatement into register of building draughtsmen"}},{"id":"BN-S-18-2019-E-APEQS-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2019-A501","no":501,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 501."},"text":{"en":"(1) A registered building draughtsman whose name has been removed from the register pursuant to this Order shall, if his appeal to the Minister is allowed, be forthwith reinstated without payment of any fee, and the Registrar shall issue a certificate of registration to him.\n\n(2) A registered building draughtsman whose name has been removed from the register pursuant to this Order and who has not appealed against that order or whose appeal has been dismissed may after the expiration of not less than 3 years from the date of the order of cancellation or from the date of the decision of the appeal apply for reinstatement.\n\n(3) The Board shall, on receipt of satisfactory evidence of proper reasons for his reinstatement and on reimbursement to it of all expenditure incurred by it arising out of the proceedings leading to the cancellation of his registration and on payment of a fee of $100, issue a certificate of registration to him. Certificate of registration to be returned 50J. A registered building draughtsman whose name has been removed from the register pursuant to this Order shall, within 14 days after notification to him by registered post of the removal, surrender to the Board the certificate of registration issued to him under this Part.\". Made this 16th. day of Syawal, 1440 Hijriah corresponding to the 19th. day of June, 2019 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan.\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN, BRUNEI DARUSSALAM. Dicetak oleh Jabatan Percetakan Kerajaan, Bandar Seri Begawan BB3510, Negara Brunei Darussalam."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"APEQS AMENDMENT ORDER 2019","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-19-2016-BANKRUPTCY-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016"] = {"id":"BN-S-19-2016-BANKRUPTCY-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"破产法修正命令 2016","en":"Bankruptcy Act Amendment Order 2016","orig":null},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"S 19/2016","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2016","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《s-19-2016-bankruptcy-act-amendment-order-2016.pdf》（3 页），本次切分 3 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"s-19-2016-bankruptcy-act-amendment-order-2016.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-19-2016-BANKRUPTCY-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"Citation"},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Bankruptcy Act (Amendment) Order, 2016"}},{"id":"BN-S-19-2016-BANKRUPTCY-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of section 38 of Chapter 67"},"text":{"en":"Section 38 of the Bankruptcy Act, in this Order referred to as the Act, is amended, in subsection (1) -\n\n(a) in paragraph (b), by deleting \"and\" from the last line;\n\n(b) in paragraph (c), in the proviso, by deleting the full stop and by substituting a semicolon therefor;\n\n(c) by adding the new immediately \"(d) all amounts due in respect of contributions payable during 12 months next before, on or after the commencement of the date of the receiving order as the employer of any person under any. written law relating to employees' superannuation or provident funds or under any scheme of superannuation which is an approved scheme under any other written law or any regulations made thereunder.\". Amendment of section 71"}},{"id":"BN-S-19-2016-BANKRUPTCY-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2016-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"BRUNEI DARUSSALAM GOVERNMENT GAZETTE"},"text":{"en":"Section 71 of the Act is amended - (a/ in subsection (I), by deleting \"or any pecuniary consideration in lieu of interest, such interest or consideration\" from the second and third lines and by \", such interest\" therefor;\n\n(b) by adding the following new subsection - \"(3) For the purposes of this section, \"interest\" includes any pecuniary in lieu of interest and any penalty or late payment charge by whatever name called. \"."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"Bankruptcy Act Amendment Order 2016","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000"] = {"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":13,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"广播 TVRO 系统条例 2000","en":"BROADCASTING TVRO SYSTEM REGULATIONS 2000","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 2/2001","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2001","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000.pdf》（8 页），本次切分 13 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"Regulations, 2000 and shall be deemed to have commenced on the 1st. March,"},"text":{"en":"These Regulations may be cited as the Broadcasting (TVRO System) Interpretation."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"\"broadcasting television receiver\" means any apparatus used for the visual"},"text":{"en":"In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires - and aural reception in monochrome or colour of any broadcasting service (but does not include any TVRO system); \"licence\" means a licence to install, import, offer for sale, sell or have in possession with a view to sale, operate or have on any premises a TVRO system on or by which broadcasting services are received; \"telecommunication\" has the same meaning as in the Telecommunications Act (Chapter 54); \"TVRO system\" means any apparatus (including dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus capable of direct reception of any broadcast matter emitted from or passing through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial space. Application for licence."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"text":{"en":"(1) Every application by a person for a licence shall be made in writing or in such manner as the Minister may specify.\n\n(2) In the case of an application for a licence to install, operate or have on any premises a TVRO system, the applicant shall specify the premises in which the applicant intends to install or operate the TVRO system and furnish such other information as the Minister may require.\n\n(3) In the case of an application for a licence to import, offer for sale, sell or have in possession with a view to sale a TVRO system, the applicant shall specify the amount and specification of the TVRO system to be imported, offered for sale or sold or in his possession with a view to sale and furnish such other information as the Minister may require. Fees."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"text":{"en":"(1) The fees for a licence shall be as specified in the Second Schedule.\n\n(2) The Minister may waive, wholly or partly, either generally or in any particular case, the payment of any fees specified in the Second Schedule. Period of licence."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"A licence shall, unless earlier revoked, be valid fof a period of 12 months"},"text":{"en":"A licence shall, unless earlier revoked, be valid fof a period of 12 months from the first day of the month in which the licence is issued. Replacement of licence."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"heading":{"en":"destroyed or defaced, the Minister may, subject to sub-regulation (2), on payment"},"text":{"en":"(1) If the Minister is satisfied that any licence issued by him has been lost, of a fee of $2, issue a duplicate licence in place thereof.\n\n(2) No duplicate licence shall be issued under this regulation in place of a defaced licence unless the defaced licence is surrendered to the Minister for cancellation. Licence non-transferable."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"A licensee shall not transfer, assign or dispose of his licence. Revocation of licence."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"heading":{"en":"failure by the licensee to comply with any of the provisions of the Act or these"},"text":{"en":"The Minister may, by notice in writing, revoke a licence on the ground of Regulations or with any conditions of the licence. Conditions of licence."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"heading":{"en":"{a) the licensee shall not install, operate or have a TVRO system on any"},"text":{"en":"(1) Every licence shall be subject to the following conditionspremises except on the premises specified in the licence;\n\n(b) the TYRO system in respect of which the licence is issued shall not be operated for the purpose of telecommunication or transmitting broadcast matter;\n\n(c) the licence shall, in accordance with any written law, obtain such permits, licences or other authorisation from other public authorities as may be necessary for or in connection with the lawful installation or operation of the TYRO system.\n\n(2) Without prejudice to sub-regulation (1), the Minister may impose such additional conditions as he thinks fit. Operating a TVRO system."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"heading":{"en":"interfere with the efficient or convenient working or maintenance of any"},"text":{"en":"(1) No TYRO system shall be operated in a manner which interferes or may telephone, telegraph or power line which existed at the time of installation of such TYRO system.\n\n(2) No licensee shall work any TYRO system in such manner as knowingly to cause interference or disturbance to reception by any other broadcasting apparatus licensed under the Act, the Telecommunications Act (Chapter 54) or any regulations made thereunder.\n\n(3) No licensee shall intercept any signal, sign, writing, image, sound or intelligence of any nature transmitted which is not intended for reception by the general public. International telecommunications agreements. _,-"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"heading":{"en":"the provisions of the International Telecommunications Convention and any"},"text":{"en":"A licensee shall, in the installation or operation of a TYRO system, observe bilateral or multilateral telecommunication agreements in force and the regulations pertaining to the operation of TYRO systems that are made under that Convention and agreements. Modifications to TVRO systems etc."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"text":{"en":"( 1) A licensee of a TYRO system shall not -\n\n(a) modify or alter any apparatus constituting the TYRO system; or\n\n(b) change the location of that TYRO system except with the approval of the Minister. lOth. JANUARY# 2001\n\n(2) If there is any change in the number of broadcast television receivers in his possession connected to a TVRO system or a change in the location of any such broadcast television receiver, the licensee of that TVRO system shall forthwith inform the Minister in writing of such change. Non-operation of TVRO system."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2001-BROADCASTING-TVRO-SYSTEM-REGULATIONS-2000-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"heading":{"en":"licence is issued, he shall not sell, offer for sale or otherwise dispose of the TVRO"},"text":{"en":"When a licensee ceases to operate the TVRO system in respect of which his system or any part thereof except with the approval of the Minister.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\nLESEN PENJUAL ALAT PENYIARAN BROADCASTING APPARATUS SELLER'S LICENCE Issued in accordance with section 23 of the Broadcasting Act Nombor Lesen Tarikh Dikeluarkan Tarikh Mansuh (Licence Number): (Date of Issue): (Expiry Date): Lesen ini dikeluarkan kepada (This Licence is issued to): Alamat Persuratan (Correspondence Address): Alamat Perniagaan (Business Address): * Lesen ini tidak boleh dipindah milik * This Licence is non-trdnsferable Bayaran Lesen Bil. Resit Tarikh (Licence Fee): (Receipt No.): (Date): bp. Menteri yang bertanggungjawab bagi perkara-perkara penyiaran. KEBENARAN MBNGIMPORT ALAT~ALAT PENYIARAN Dikeluarkan menurut bab 23 dari Akta Penyiaran\n\nIMPORT PERMIT FOR BROADCASTING APPARATUS Issued in accordance with section 23 of the Broadcasting Act I Kebenaran ini dikeluarkan kepada Tarikh Tarikh Mansuh /This Permit is issued to}: Dikeluarkan (Expiry Date}: {Date of Issue}: * Kebenaran ini tidak boleh dipindah milik dan hanya sah bagi satu pengimportan sahaja (This Permit is not-transferable and only valid for a single import} Alamat Persuratan {Correspondence Address}: Alamat Penyimpanan Alat Penyiaran Yang Diimport {Storage Address for Imported Broadcasting Apparatus}: Keterangan Jumlah & Spesifi.kasi Alat Penyiaran Yang Hendak Diimport {Details of Amount & Specification of Broadcasting Apparatus to be Imported}: Rujukan Kebenaran Bil. Resit Tarikh {Permit Reference}: {Receipt No.}: {Date}: bp. Menteri yang bertanggungjawab bagi perkara-perkara penyiaran.\n\nLESEN PENGENDALIAN ALAT PENYIARAN\n\nOPERATION OF BROADCASTING APPARATUS LICENCE Issued in accordance with section 23 of the Broadcasting Act N ombor Lesen Tarikh Dikeluarkan Tarikh Mansuh {Licence Number}: {Date of Issue}: {Expiry Date}: i Lesen ini dikeluarkan kepada {This Licence is issued to}: Alamat Persuratan {Correspondence Address}: Alamat Pemasangan {Installation Address}: * Lesen ini tidak boleh dipindah milik * This Licence is non-try:msferable Bayaran Lesen Bil. Resit Tarikh {Licence Fee}: {Receipt No.}: (Date}: bp. Menteri yang bertanggungjawab bagi perkara-perkara penyiaran. lOth. 2001\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE The fees payable under regulation 4 are as follows (il for the installation, operation or having on any premises a TVRO system for private viewing $360.00 per annum\n\n(ii) for the installation, operation or having on any business or commercial premises (including restaurants, eating-houses and coffee-shops) a TVRO system $500.00 per annum ·\n\n(iii) for the installation, operation or having in any hotels, service apartments or other commercial lodgings of a similar nature a TVRO system .$1,200.00 per annum\n\n(iv) for the sale of a TVRO system $1,500.00 per annum Made this 16th. day of Ramadan, 1421 Hijriah corresponding to the 13th. day of December, 2000. PEHIN ORANG KAYA LAlLA SETIA BAKTI DIRAJA DATO LAlLA UTAMA HAJI AWANG ISA BIN PEHIN DATU PERDANA MANTER! DATO LAlLA UTAMA HAJI IBRAHIM Minister responsible for broadcasting matters, Prime Minister's Office, Brunei Darussalam."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"BROADCASTING TVRO SYSTEM REGULATIONS 2000","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498"] = {"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":27,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"雇员信托基金局命令 2016 第四附表第 27 条","en":"SEC 27 FOURTH SCHEDULE OF THE TABUNG AMANAH PEKERJA BOARD ORDER 2016","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 2/2016","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2016","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-PEKERJA-BOARD-ORDER-2016.pdf》（19 页），本次切分 27 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-PEKERJA-BOARD-ORDER-2016.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"Citation, commencement and long title"},"text":{"en":"{1) This Order may be cited as the Tabung Amanah Pekerja Board Order, 2016 and shall be deemed to have commenced on 1st April 2014.\n\n(2) The long title of this Order is \"An Order to establish and incorporate the Amanah Pekerja Board and to provide for all matters connected therewith or i\\}cidental thereto\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires means the Tabung Amanah Pekerja Board established under 3; of Directors\" means the Board of Directors referred to in section 5; means the Chairman of the Board of Directors referred to in 5(2){a); means a committee appointed under section 9{ 1 J; Chairmen\" means the Deputy Chairmen of the Board of Directors to in section 5(2){b); \"Fund\" means the Tabung Amanah Pekerja Fund established under \"Managing Director\" means the Managing Director appointed under means a member of the Board of Directors referred to in means the Minister of Finance.\n\nAMANAH PEKERJA BOARD of Board"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"Establishment of Board"},"text":{"en":"There is hereby established a board known as the Tabung Amanah Pekerja which shall be a body corporate with perpetual succession and a common seal and shall, by that name, be capable of {a} suing and being sued; {b) acquiring, owning, holding, developing or disposing of property, both movable and immovable; and {c) doing all such other acts or things as a body corporate may lawfully do. seal"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"Common seal"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Board shall have a common seal and such seal may be changed, altered or made anew as the Board thinks fit.\n\n(2) All deeds and other documents requiring the seal of the Board shall be sealed with the common seal of the Board.\n\n(3) All instruments to which the common seal is affixed shall be signed by any two members generally or specially authorised by the Board for .that purpose.\n\n(4) The Board may, by resolution or otherwise in writing, appoint an officer of the Board or any other person either generally or in any particular case to or sign on behalf of the Board any agreement or other instrument not seal in relation to any matter within the powers of the Board.\n\n(5) All courts, judges and persons acting judicially shall take judicial notice of the common seal of the Board affixed to any document and shall presume that it was duly affixed. of Directors"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"Board of Directors"},"text":{"en":"(1) There shall be a Board of Directors which shall be responsible for the policy and general administration of the affairs and business of the Board.\n\n(2) The Board of Directors shall consist of the following members (a} a Chairman; {b) not more than two Deputy Chairmen; (cJ such number of other directors, of whom not less than five shall be representatives of the Government, as His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan may appoint.\n\n(3) the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan shall appoint one of the directors to be the Managing Director.\n\n(4) The First Schedule shall have effect with respect to the Board, its and proceedings. Director"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"Managing Direcfor"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The Managing Director shall be entrusted with the day to day administration of the Board and the Fund, preparation of programmes, schemes the consideration of the Board and the implementation of decisions of the Board.\n\n(2) The Managing Director shall be an employee of the Board on such and conditions of service as His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan may decide. · (3l The Managing Director shall be answerable to the Board of Directors for his acts and decisions. of Minister"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"Directions of Minister"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Minister may give the Board such directions in writing, not with the provisions of this Order, as he thinks fit, as to exercise of any power or the performance of any functions conferred or imposed on it by this and the Board shall give effect to any such direction.\n\n(2) The Board shall furnish the Minister with such information with respect property, the exercise of its powers and performance of its functions as he may require. of powers"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"Delegation of powers"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The Board of Directors may, in respect of a specified matter or class of in writing, delegate to any person or committee of the Board of Directors the exercise of any power or the performance of any function conferred or on it by this Order, except for the power of delegation conferred by this\n\n(2) A delegation under subsection (1) may be(a) subject to such conditions as may be determined by the Board of the instrument of delegation; and\n\n(b) revoked or varied by a subsequent order made in the same manner.\n\n(3) The Board of Directors may continue to exercise any power and any function conferred or imposed on it by this Order notwithstanding the delegation by it of such power or function."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"Committees"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Board of Directors may, in its discretion, appoint committees of persons who are members or otherwise, for purposes which, in the opinion of the Board of Directors, would be better regulated and managed by such committees.\n\n(2) The Board of Directors may define or vary the terms of reference of the\n\n(3) Subject to this Order and to the control of the Board of Directors, each may regulate its procedure in such manner as the committee thinks fit. of staff"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The Board may appoint and employ for such terms of office and on such of service as the Board may determine such other officers, employees and consultants as may be necessary for the effective performance of its\n\nAND POWERS of Fund"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"heading":{"en":"Establishment of Fund"},"text":{"en":"For the purposes of this Order, there shall be established a fund known as Amanah Pekerja Fund into which shall be paid all contributions to the trusts established under the written laws set out in the Second Schedule and out of which shall be met all payments authorised to be paid under those written laws."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"heading":{"en":"Functions and duties of Board"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Board shall be the trustee of the Fund and all monies of the Fund may be(a) deposited in a bank or banks approved by the Board;\n\n(b) invested in any of the investments authorised by the Government for the investment of trust money and the Board shall have power to convert the same into cash; or {cj used for the purchase of any property and for the construction of for the purposes of the Board and to let the buildings or part for the purposes of deriving income therefrom and the Board may dispose of all or any part of those property and buildings.\n\n(2) The Board shall be charged with the general administration of the laws set out in the Second Schedule and the exercise of the functions and imposed on the Board by those written laws.\n\n(3) The Board may authorise any person to assist the Board in the exercise of its functions and duties under the written laws set out in the Second Schedule, generally or in a particular case. of Board"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"( 1) to this Order, the Board may carry on such activities as appear to the Board to be advantageous, necessary or convenient for it to carry on, for or in connection with, the discharge of its functions under this Order.\n\n(2) The Board shall, in addition to its powers and functions set out in this exercise all the powers conferred or imposed on the Board under the laws set out in the Second Schedule.\n\nPROVISIONS"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Financial year"},"text":{"en":"The financial year of the Fund shall be determined by the Board. and financial statements"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Accounts and financial statements"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Board shall keep proper accounts and records of its transactions and affairs and shall do all things necessary to ensure that all payments out of its are correctly made and properly authorised and that adequate control is over the assets of, or in the custody of, the Board and over the expenditure incurred by it.\n\n(2) The Board shall, as soon as practicable after the close of each financial year, cause financial statements in respect of that year to be prepared and to the auditor of the Board."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Expenses"},"text":{"en":"All expenses incurred by the Board including the cost of auditing the of the trusts established under the written laws set out in the Second shall be defrayed out of the monies of the Fund."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Audit"},"text":{"en":"(1) The accounts of the Fund shall be audited at least once annually by {a} the Auditor or (b} any person who has been authorised to perform the duties required by the Companies Act (Chapter 39) to be performed by an auditor, who shall be appointed annually by the Board: that where the accounts of the Fund have been audited by a appointed under subsection (1){b}, the report submitted under that may be verified by the Auditor General before it is submitted to the Board.\n\n(2) The auditor shall in his report state {a} whether the financial statements show fairly the financial and the state of affairs of the Board;\n\n(b) whether proper accounting and other records have been kept, including records of all assets of the Board whether purchased or otherwise;\n\n(c) whether expenditure and investment of moneys and the and disposal of assets by the Board during the financial year were in accordance with the provisions of this Order; and {d) such other matter arising from the audit as he considers necessary. auditor"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Powers of auditor"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The auditor or any person authorised by him shall be entitled at all time to full and free access to all accounting and other records relating, directly or indirectly, to the financial transactions of the Board.\n\n(2) The auditor or a person authorised by him may make copies of, or make extracts from, any such accounting and other records.\n\n(3) The auditor or any person authorised by him may require any person to him with such information which that person possesses or has access to as the auditor or any duly authorised person considers necessary for the purposes of the functions of the auditor under this Order."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"The Board shall, as soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, to the Minister an annual report on the activities of the Board during the financial year, and the Minister shall cause a copy of every such annual to be presented to His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan.\n\nPARTV from personal liability"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Protection from personal liability"},"text":{"en":"No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie against any member, officer or of the Board or any other person acting under the direction of the Board is done in good faith or intended to be done in execution or purported execution of this Order or of the written laws set out in the Second Schedule."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Public servants"},"text":{"en":"All members, officers and employees of the Board shall be deemed to be servants for the purposes of the Penal Code !Chapter 22). of Schedules"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of Schedules"},"text":{"en":"The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang by order published in the Gazette, amend the Schedules."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Regulations"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and make regulations which are necessary or expedient for giving and carrying out the provisions of this Order, including any other thing to be or which may be prescribed under this Order, and for the due thereof.\n\n(2) Such regulations may include such incidental, consequential and supplementary provisions as the Minister considers necessary or expedient. of functions, property etc."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"The provisions of the Third Schedule shall have effect for the purpose of the to the Board of functions, property and for other transitional purposes the Third Schedule."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Transitional"},"text":{"en":"On the date of commencement of this Order {a} the Lembaga Tabung Amanah Pekerja established under the Amanah Pekerja Act (Chapter 167) shall be known as the Tabung Pekerja Board established under section 3;\n\n(b) the Tabung Amanah Pekerja established under the Tabung Amanah Act (Chapter 167) shall be known as the Tabung Amanah Pekerja Fund established under section 11."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"heading":{"en":"Savings"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Managing Director appointed under section 3A of the Tabung Pekerja Act (Chapter 167] immediately before the commencement of this shall be deemed for the purposes of this Order to have been appointed as the Managing Director on the commencement of this Order.\n\n(2) The members of the Lembaga Tabung Amanah Pekerja appointed under 4(2) of the Tabung Amanah Pekerja Act (Chapter 167) immediately before the commencement of this Order shall be deemed for the purposes of this Order to have been appointed to be members of the Tabung Amanah Pekerja Board on the commencement of this Order. Consequential and related amendments to other written laws"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2016-SEC-27-FOURTH-SCHEDULE-OF-THE-TABUNG-AMANAH-C0C498-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"The provisions of the other written laws specified in the first column of the Schedule are amended in the manner set out in second column thereof.\n\nSCHEDULE (section 5(4])\n\nAND PROCEEDINGS OF BOARD OF DIRECTORS Terms and conditions of office"}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"SEC 27 FOURTH SCHEDULE OF THE TABUNG AMANAH PEKERJA BOARD ORDER 2016","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AME-9C4F85"] = {"id":"BN-S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AME-9C4F85","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"宗教理事会与卡迪法庭法修正命令 2026","en":"RELIGIOUS COUNCIL AND KADIS COURTS ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 2026","orig":null},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"S 2/2026","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2026.pdf》（3 页），本次切分 4 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2026.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AME-9C4F85-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Religious Council and Kadis Courts Act (Amendment) Order, 2026."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AME-9C4F85-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"of section 2 of Chapter 77"},"text":{"en":"of the Religious Council and Kadis Courts Act, in this Order referred to as the Act, is amended by inserting the following new definition immediately after the definition of \"fitrah\" - \"Fund\" means the Mosque Construction Fund established by section 123A;\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AME-9C4F85-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"of section 107"},"text":{"en":"of the Act is amended by inserting \"and any fund established by this Act\" immediately after \"Endowment Fund\" in the second and fifth lines. of new sections 123A and 123B"}},{"id":"BN-S-2-2026-E-RELIGIOUS-COUNCIL-AND-KADIS-COURTS-ACT-AME-9C4F85-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"KERAJAAN NEGARA BRUNEI DARUSSALAM"},"text":{"en":"amended by inserting the following two new sections immediately after section 123 - Construction Fund 123A. (1) It is hereby established a fund called the Mosque Construction Fund for the purposes of this Act into which shall be paid(a} any money contributed voluntarily to the Fund; (b} any money obtained through the implementation of any of the Fund; and\n\n(c) subject to the approval of the Majlis, any sum contributed specifically for the construction of mosques under other written the sums contributed specifically for a particular\n\n(2) All moneys in the Fund shall be vested in the Majlis.\n\n(3) All moneys contributed to the fund for the construction of the the Mosque Construction Fund Rules, 2026 is in force, together with the income therefrom, shall be a part of the Fund.\n\n(4) The Majlis may appoint a board, committee or secretariat to receive, collect, manage or control the money contributed specifically for the construction of mosques.\n\n(5) Nothing in this Act shall be interpreted as prohibiting the Majlis from accepting contributions for the Fund from any non-Muslim. of Fund 123B. The moneys of the Fund shall be used - (aJ to construct mosques in Brunei Darussalam and other works approved by the Majlis including funeral room, library, multi-purpose hall, mosque fences and lots; (bf to extend, restore, maintain, renovate or reconstruct any or any part thereof; (cf if necessary, for takaful financing for any mosque building; and (df any other requirements as the Majlis may determine.\". Made this 18th. day of Rejab, 1447 Hijriah corresponding to the 8th. day of January, 2026 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN, DARUSSALAM."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"RELIGIOUS COUNCIL AND KADIS COURTS ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 2026","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988"] = {"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":24,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"文莱达鲁萨兰大学紧急状态命令 1988","en":"EMERGENCY UNIVERSITI BRUNEI DARUSSALAM ORDER 1988","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 20/1988","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"1988","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-20_1988_E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988.pdf》（28 页），本次切分 24 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-20_1988_E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"The provisions of the Constitution shall, upon the appointed University"},"text":{"en":"There is hereby established, in accordance with the provisions Establishment of this Constitution, a University with the name and style of Universi-of University as body ti Brunei Darussalam by which name and style the Chancellor, the Pro-corporate. Chancellor, the Vice-Chancellor, and the members for the time being of the Council and the Senate are hereby constituted a body corporate with perpetual succession, and with full power and authority under such name -\n\n(a) to have and use a common seal and from time to time to break, change, alter and make anew such seals as it shall think fit ;\n\n(b) for the purposes of this Constitution and subject to the statutes and regulations, to purchase any property, movable or immovable, and to take, accept and hold any such property which may become vested in it by virtue of any such purchase, or by any exchange, grant, donation, lease, testamentary disposition or otherwise ;\n\n(c) to sell, mortgage, lease, exchange or otherwise dispose of any such property ; and\n\n(d) to exercise and perform, in accordance with the provisions of this Constitution and of the statutes and regulations, all powers and duties conferred or imposed upon the University by such provisions. Powers of 4. ( 1) The University shall, subject to the provisions of this ConstituUniversity. tion, have the following powers -\n\n(a) to provide courses of instruction, to hold examinations, to make provisions for research, and to take such other steps as may appear necessary or desirable for the advancement and dissemination of knowledge ;\n\n(b) to confer degrees and diplomas including external degress and diplomas upon persons who have followed courses of study approved by the University and have satisfied such other requirements as may be prescribed by statute or regulation ;\n\n(c) to recognize the degrees and diplomas of other institutions of higher learning for the purpose of admission to the courses and examinations of the University and of the award of higher degrees on holders of such degrees or diplomas or on graduates of the University on such conditions as may be prescribed by statute or regulation ;\n\n(d) to confer degrees upon teachers of the University who have satisfied such requirements as may be prescribed by statute or regulation ;\n\n(e) to confer honorary degrees on persons who have contributed to the advancement or dissemination of knowledge or who have rendered distinguished public service ;\n\n(f) to grant certificates to persons who have attained proficiency in any branch or branches of knowledge ;\n\n(g) to institute chairs, lectureships, and other posts and offices, and to make appointments thereto ;\n\n(h) to establish a University printing press and to publish books and other matters ;\n\n(i) to erect, equip and maintain libraries, laboratories, museums, lecture halls, halls of residence and all other buildings required for the purposes of the University ; U) to institute and award fellowships, scholarships, exhibitions, bursaries, medals, prizes and other titles, distinctions, awards and other forms of assistance towards the advancement and dissemination of knowledge ;\n\n(k) to invest in land or securities (whether authorised as trustee investments or not) such funds as may be vested in it for the purpose of endowment, whether for general or special purposes, or such other funds as may not be immediately required for current expenditure, with power from time to time to vary any such investment and to deposit any moneys for the time being uninvested with any bank either upon fixed deposit or upon current account ;\n\n(1) to enter into contracts, to appoint such staff and to establish such trusts, as may be required for the purposes of the University ;\n\n(m) to appoint, promote and discipline officers, teachers and staff of the University ;\n\n(n) to regulate the conditions of service of the staff of the University, including schemes of service, salary scales, leave and discipline ;\n\n(o) to regulate and provide for the residence of officers, teachers, staff and students of the University and the welfare and discipline of teachers, staff and students ;\n\n(p) to demand and receive such fees as may from time to time be prescribed by the Council, and\n\n(g) to do all such acts and things, whether or not incidental to the powers aforesaid as may be requisite in order to further instruction, research, finance, administration, welfare and discipline in the University.\n\n(2) If His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan is satisfied that it is necessary to confer an honorary degree upon a foreign dignitary, on the direction of His Majesty the University shall confer such degree as stated in the direction."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"The University shall keep at the office mentioned in section 4 Copies of"},"text":{"en":"The University shall observe such instructions as His Majesty Admission of The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan may give with regard to the admis-students or appointment sion of students or appointment of staff of the University and such in-of staff. structions may include the reservation of such number of University places or appointments as His Majesty may think fit for persons who are subjects of His Majesty under section 4 of the Brunei Nationality Act."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"text":{"en":"(1) The common seal of the University shall be such seal as may The Seal of be approved by the Council, and such seal may in like manner from the University. time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew.\n\n(2) The common seal of the University shall be kept in the custody of the Bursar.\n\n(3) The common seal of the University shall not be affixed to any instrument other than a degree diploma or certificate of the University except in the presence of the Vice-Chancellor and one other member of the Council who shall sign their names in the instrument in token of such presence ; and such signature shall be sufficient evidence that such seal was duly and properly affixed and that the same is the lawful seal of the University.\n\n(4) The seal of the University shall be officially and judicially noticed.\n\n(5) Any document or instrument which (if executed by a person not being a body corporate) will not require to be under seal may in like manner be executed on behalf of the University by an officer or any person generally or specifically authorised for the purpose by the Council.\n\nTHE PRINCIPAL OFFICERS OF THE UNIVERSITY The 7. ( 1) There shall be a Chancellor who shall be His Majesty The Sultan Chancellor. and Yang Di-Pertuan.\n\n(2) The Chancellor shall be the Head of the University and shall have the following functions -\n\n(a) to preside when present at meetings of the Council and any Convocation of the University ;\n\n(b) to receive an annual report on the University from the ViceChancellor ;\n\n(c) to receive such special reports as the Council may submit ; and\n\n(d) to exercise such powers and duties as may be conferred upon him by this Constitution or any statu\"te or regulation. The Pro-8. (1) The Chancellor may appoint such persons to be Pro-Chancellors Chancellor. as he may consider proper.\n\n(2) If for any reason the Chancellor is unable to exercise any of his functions under this Constitution or any statute or regulations, he may authorise any of the Pro-Chancellors to exercise such functions on his behalf.\n\n(3) Every Pro-Chancellor shall hold office during the pleasure of the Chancellor."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"(1) There shall be a Vice-Chancellor who shall be appointed by The Vice· His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan . Chancellor.\n\n(2) The Vice-Chancellor shall be the principal executive and academic officer of the University.\n\n(3) It shall be the duty of the Vice-Chancellor :\n\n(a) to see that the provisions of this Constitution and the statutes and regulations are observed, and he shall have all such powers as may be necessary for this purpose and , in particular, to ensure that every authority or committee keeps within its powers or terms of reference ; and\n\n(b) to exercise, subject to the provisions of this Constitution, general supervision over the arrangements for instruction, research, finance, administration, welfare and discipline in the University, and to exercise such other powers as may be conferred upon him by this Constitution and any statute or regulation .\n\n(4) The term of office and other conditions of service of the ViceChancellor shall be determined by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, after consultation with the Council, and shall be binding on the University.\n\n(5) Subject to the provisions of this Constitution or any statute or regulations, the Vice-Chancellor shall be ex-officio chairman of every authority of the University."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"for the purposes of paragraph (f) of sub-section ( 1) of section 10 of the University"},"text":{"en":"(1) There shall be at least one Deputy Vice-Chancellor appointed Depuly Vice· by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, and any fit and proper Chancellor. person may be so appointed either from within or without the University ; the term of office and other conditions of service of a Deputy ViceChancellor shall be determined by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, after consultation with the Council and shall be binding on the University.\n\n(2) The duties of a Deputy Vice-Chancellor shall be prescribed by the Vice-Chancellor or by this Constitution or any statute or regulations.\n\n(3) If for any substantial period the Vice-Chancelk>r is unable by reason of illness, leave of absence or any other cause to exercise any of the functions of his office, the following arrangements shall apply :\n\n(a) where the Vice-Chancellor has been appointed in an ex-officio capacity, the person acting or discharging the functions of that ex-officio capacity shall be deemed to be acting as Vice-Chancellor ;\n\n(b) where the Vice-Chancellor has been appointed by name, the Deputy Vice-Chancellor or, if there is more than one Deputy Vice-Chancellor, such one of them as may be named by the Vice-Chancellor shall exercise such functions ; and in the event of the absence or disability of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor or all the Deputy Vice-Chancellors (if there be more than one) His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan shall, after consultation with the ViceChancellor or the Council if such consultation cannot be held with the Vice-Chancellor for whatever cause, make such temporary arrangements as His Majesty may think fit for the exercise of the functions of the Vice-Chancellor. Registrar and 11. There shall be a Registrar and Secretary, a Chief Librarian and Secretary, a Bursar, who shall be whole-time principal officers of the University Chief Librarian, and appointed by the Council and who shall have such powers and duties Bursar. as may be prescribed by statute. Dean of a 12. For the purpose of this Constitution, the Dean of a Faculty Faculty and or the Head of a Centre or School shall be deemed to be a principal Head of a officer of the University. Centre or School. Other 13. The University may appoint such other principal officers as principal may be prescribed by statute. officers.\n\nTHE UNIVERSITY AUTHORITIES The 14. (1) The authorities of the University shall be the Council, the authorities. Senate, the Board of an Institution, the Boards of Selection, the Board of Student Welfare, and such other bodies as may be prescribed by statute as authorities of the University.\n\n(2) Subject to the provisions of this Constitution, the composition, powers and procedure of the authorities shall be prescribed by statute. The Council. 15. ( 1) The Council shall consist of :\n\n(a) the Vice-Chancellor, who shall be Chairman ;\n\n(b) three persons appointed by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan on the advice of the Vice-Chancellor ;\n\n(c) one person elected by the Senate from among its members other than the Vice-Chancellor or the Deputy ViceChancellors ;\n\n(d) the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Finance (or his representative) ;\n\n(e) the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Education (or his representative) ;\n\n(f) the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Development (or his representative) ;\n\n(g) the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Religious Affairs (or his representative) ;\n\n(h) the Attorney-General (or his representative) ;\n\n(i) the Director of Establishment (or his representative) ; and Ul one representative of the Guild of Graduates of Universiti Brunei Darussalam elected from among its members provided that such representative is not a full-time staff member of the University.\n\n(2) The Registrar and Secretary shall be Secretary to the Council.\n\n(3) The Chairman of the Council shall appoint a Deputy Chairman of the Council from among the members of the Council other than the representative of the Senate, and during any absence of the Chairman from any sitting the Deputy Chairman shall preside over the sitting, and, if the Deputy Chairman is also absent, such other member as may be elected by the members present shall sit as Chairman of the Council.\n\n(4) The Deputy Chairman shall vacate his office on ceasing to be a member of the Council.\n\n(5) The Deputy Vice-Chancellor may attend meetings of the Council but shall have no vote."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"The Council shall be the executive body of the University and may Powers of lhe exercise all the powers conferred on the University, save in so far as Council. they are by this Constitution or the statutes and regulations conferred on some other authority or body or on some other officer of the University. Provided that -\n\n(a) no resolution shall be passed by the Council relating to any matter within the powers of the Senate unless the Senate has first been given the opportunity of recording and transmitting to the Council its opinion thereon ; and\n\n(b) no member of the Council who is a member of the teaching staff (other than a principal officer) shall take part in the proceedings of the Council when it is holding discussions or making decisions on the appointment, promotion and other matters relating to the service of any member of the teaching staff. The Senate. 1 7. ( 1) The Senate shall consist of :\n\n(a) the Vice-Chancellor, who shall be Chairman ;\n\n(b) the Deputy Vice-Chancellor ;\n\n(c) the heads of institutions ;\n\n(d) the heads of teaching departments ;\n\n(e) the professors of the University but not including visiting professors ; and\n\n(f) such other persons as may be prescribed by statute.\n\n(2) The Vice-Chancellor may appoint a Deputy Vice-Chancellor to deputise for him as Chairman at any meeting of the Senate if the Vice-Chancellor is unable to attend the meeting.\n\n(3) The Registrar and Secretary shall be Secretary to the Senate.\n\n(4) The Senate shall be the academic body of the University and, subject to the provisions of this Constitution, the statutes and regulations, shall have the control and general direction of instruction, research and examination, and the award of degrees, diplomas and certificates.\n\n(5) In the performance of its duties, functions and responsibilities, the Senate may delegate any of its duties, functions and responsibilities to its members or a committee consisting of its members. The Faculties, 18. (1) The University shall be divided into such number and names Centres and of Faculties, Centres and Schools as may be prescribed by statute . Schools.\n\n(2) The Board of a Faculty, Centre or School shall be responsible to the Senate for the organisation of instruction in the subject of study within the purview of the Faculty, Centre or School, as the case may be, and may exercise such other functions as may be conferred on it by statute or regulation.\n\n(3) The composition of the Board of a Faculty, Centre or School shall be as prescribed by statute."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) Subject to any statute the Council shall, on the advice of the Appoinlmenl Vice-Chancellor, appoint -of heads and depuly heads of inslilulions\n\n(a) a Dean in respect of each Faculty and, where necessary, and heads of at least one Deputy Dean ; leaching deparlmenls.\n\n(b) a head in respect of a Centre or School and, where necessary , at least one deputy head, who shall be styled by such title as may be prescribed by statute or regulation ; and\n\n(c) a head in respect of each teaching department where such teaching departments are established in a Faculty, Centre or School.\n\n(2) The Dean of a Faculty or head of a Centre or School shall be chairman of the Board of the Faculty, Centre or School, as the case may be.\n\n(3) The Dean of a Faculty or head of a Centre or School or head of teaching department shall be responsible for the organisation of instruction of courses or subjects falling under the purview of the Faculty, Centre, School or teaching department, as the case may be, and sha ll exercise such other functions as may be vested upon him by statute or regulation or as may be directed by the Vice-Chancellor.\n\n(4) In the absence of the Dean of a Faculty or head of a Centre or School, on leave or for any other reason, it shall be lawful for the Deputy Dean or deputy head or, if there is more than one Deputy Dean or deputy head, such one of them as may be named by the ViceChancellor, to exercise any of the functions of the Dean of the Faculty or head of the Centre or School, as the case may be.\n\n(5) The Dean or Deputy Dean of a Faculty or head or deputy head of a Centre or School or the head of a teaching department appointed under sub-section ( 1). as the case may be, shall be appointed for a period not exceeding two years but shall be eligible for re-appointment.\n\n(6) Notwithstanding the provisions of sub-section (5), the Council may, on the advice of the Vice-Chancellor, revoke any appointment made under this section without assigning any reason .\n\n(7) Notwithstanding the other provisions of this section, the ViceChancellor may, pending any appointment to be made by the Council under sub-section (1) , appoint any person to exercise the functions of the Dean or Deputy Dean of a Faculty or head or deputy head of a Centre or School or head of a teaching department, as the case may be."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"( 1) A Board of Selection for teachers shall, subject to any statute, Boards of consist of-Seleclion for leachcrs.\n\n(a) the Vice-Chancellor, who shall be Chairman ;\n\n(b) one member of the Council appointed by the Council ;\n\n(c) the Dean of the Faculty or head of the Centre or School concerned ; and\n\n(d) one member of the Senate appointed by the Senate.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding the provisions of sub-section (1), the ViceChancellor may appoint the Deputy Vice-Chancellor to deputies for him as Chairman at any meeting of a Board of Selection which has been convened to fill an appointment other than that to a chair.\n\n(3) The association of external experts with the making of appointment may be prescribed by statute. Boards of 21. The composition of Boards of Selection for appointments other Selection for than teachers shall be as prescribed by statute. other appointments. The Board of 22. (1) There shall be established a Board of Student Welfare which Student shall consist of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor or, if there is more than Welfare. one Deputy Vice-Chancellor, such one of them as may be named by the Vice-Chancellor as Chairman and such other persons as may be appointed by the Vice-Chancellor.\n\n(2) The Board of Student Welfare shall have such powers as may be prescribed by Statute. Guild of 23. (1) Subject to the approval of the Council, it shall be lawful fojc Graduates. not less than thirty graduates of the University to form and establish an association to be known as the Guild of Graduates.\n\n(2) The Guild of Graduates shall be governed and administered in accordance with its constitution and rules made by it and no such constitution and rules so made or any amendments thereto shall come into force unless and until approval thereof shall have first been obtained from the Council. Term of office 24. ( 1) Except as may be prescribed by this Constitution or by any of members of statute, the term of office of a person elected or appointed to be a authorities. member of an authority, otherwise than shall be three years : ex-officio, Provided that :\n\n(a) where the person is elected or appointed because he holds an office or is a member of some other authority or body, he shall cease to be a member of the authority if before the expiry of his term of office he ceases to hold such office or to be a member of such authority or body ;\n\n(b) where the person is appointed by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan to be a member of any authority, His Majesty may, if he deems fit, revoke the appointment at any time during the term of such appointment ; and\n\n(c) a person who retires at the end of his term of office shall be eligible for re-election or reappointment if he is otherwise qualified.\n\n(2) When a person is a member of an authority ex-officio, a person appointed to act for him shall be a member of the authority ex-officio so long as he is so acting and is otherwise qualified.\n\n(3) The decision of an authority shall be valid notwithstanding any vacancy among its members."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"( 1) Subject to the provisions of this Constitution and to any statute Majority or regulations, a question at any meeting of any authority shall be decid-decision and ed by a majority of the votes of the members present. Quorum of meetings.\n\n(2) The Chairman and every member shall have and may exercise one vote each, but in the event of an equality of votes, the Chairman shall have and may exercise a second or casting vote.\n\n(3) The quorum for meetings of any authority shall be as prescribed by statute or regulations or in the Standing Orders of the authority.\n\nSTATUTES AND REGULATIONS"}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"( 1) Subject to the provisions of this Constitution, the Chancellor Statutes. may from time to time make such statute of the University as may be necessary or expedient for the administration of the affairs or for carrying out the functions of the University.\n\n(2) Without prejudice to the generality of sub-section ( 1). statutes may be made to prescribe or provide for all or any of the following matters -\n\n(a) the powers and duties of the officers of the University ;\n\n(b) the methods of appointment and the conditions of service of the officers and teachers of the University ;\n\n(c) the determination of degrees, diplomas and other academic distinctions to be conferred by the University ;\n\n(d) the management of the library and research institutes ;\n\n(e) all other matters which under this Constitution may be regulated by statute ;\n\n(f) the composition, powers, duties and procedure of the authorities of the University ;\n\n(g) matters incidental to or consequential upon any of the matters aforesaid ; and\n\n(h) all the matters within the powers of the University and not otherwise provided for by this part of this Constitution. Procedure on 27. (1) The proposal for the making of any statute or the revocation making, or amendment of any statute, shall be prepared by the Council. amending or revoking statutes. (2) A proposal for a new statute, or of any amendment to a statute, dealing' with any of the following matters, that is to say -\n\n(a) the composition, powers, duties and procedures of the Senate, the Board of a Faculty, the Board of a Centre or School, or the Board of Student Welfare ;\n\n(b) the determination of degrees, diplomas and other academic distinctions to be conferred by the University ;\n\n(c) the conditions of residence and the welfare of students ;\n\n(d) the management of the library ; and\n\n(e) all other matters within the jurisdiction of the Senate under this Constitution or any statute ; shall not be submitted to the Chancellor until it has been referred to the Senate and the Senate has reported to the Council its observations thereon. Regulations. 28. Subject to the provisions of this Constitution and the statutes, regulations may be made for all or any of the following matters -\n\n(a) the principles governing the award of degrees, diplomas and other academic dist.inctions.\n\n(b) the number and scope of examinations ;\n\n(c) the appointment, powers and duties of examiners and the conduct of examinations ;\n\n(d) the admission of students to the examinations and the degree and diploma courses of the University ;\n\n(e) the conditions of residence and the welfare of students ;\n\n(f) the fees to be charged for courses of study, residence, admission to examination, degrees and diplomas and any other fees that may be levied by the University ;\n\n(g) the management of lecture halls and laboratories ;\n\n(h) the composition, powers and duties of any Board, committee or other body not specifically provided for in this Constitution or by statute ;\n\n(i) all matters which by this Constitution or any statute may be prescribed by regulatiol).S ; and Ul all matters within the powers of the University and not otherwise provided for by this Part of this Constitution."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The Council may, subject to the provisions of this Section, Procedure on make, amend or revoke any regulations. amending makin~. or revoking\n\n(2) The draft of any regulations dealing with any matter within regulat ions. the jurisdiction of the Senate shall be proposed by the Senate ; and the Council may approve the draft or refer it back to the Senate with observations or porposals for amendment."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30."},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The Council and the Senate may each make regulations for Regulations its own procedure. for procedure of the Council and Senate.\n\n(2) The Council may make regulations for the procedure of Boards of Selection.\n\n(3) The Senate may make regulations for the procedure of the Board of a Faculty, Centre or School or of any other board or committee subject to the jurisdiction of the Senate.\n\n(4) The Senate may make regulations prescribing courses of study or syllabi or examinations.\n\n(5) Regulations may be made by an authority if it is so empowered by this Constitution or any statute. Disciplinary 31. Notwithstanding the provisions of regulations 26, 28 and 30, Provisions. statutes or regulations may be made to provide for the discipline of staff and students of the University. Publication of 32. (1) When any new statute or regulation is made, amended or restatutes and voked every such statute or regulation, amendment or revocation shall regulations. be published in the and in such other manner as Government Gazette the Council may direct.\n\n(2) The statutes and regulations of the University as amended from time to time shall be published in book form at such intervals as the Council may direct, and copies shall be made available for purchase at a reasonable price by members of the public.\n\n(3) Nothing in this section shall apply to -\n\n(a) any regulation containing only instructions to examiners or invigilators or details concerning courses of study or syllabi or examinations ;\n\n(b) any regulation which the Council resolves not to publish. Constitution, 33. In the event of - inconsistencies between (a) any statute being inconsistent with the provisions of this statutes, etc. Constitution ; or\n\n(b) any regulation being inconsistent with the provisions of this Constitution or any statute ; then the provisions of the Constitution or statute, as the case may be, shall prevail, and such statute or regulation, as the case may be, shall to the extent of the inconsistency be void.\n\nFINANCIAL PROVISIONS Standing 34. The Council shall appoint a Standing Finance Committee for Finance regulating and controlling the finances of the University. Committee. Preparation of 35. ( 1) It shall be the duty of the Bursar to prepare, in consultation Estimates and with the Registrar and Secretary, the estimates of income and expenFinancial diture of the University for each financial year for the consideration Year. of the Vice-Chancellor and submission to the Finance committee.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part of this Constitution, the financial year shall be the calendar year or such other period as the Council may determine.\n\n(3) The accounts of the University shall, as soon as may be, be balanced for the preceding financial year and an annual statement or abstract thereof shall be prepared in such form and with such information as the council may direct from time to time."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"(1) The detailed estimates of income and expenditure of the Annual University for any financial year approved by the Council shall be sub-Estimates. mitted prior to the beginning of the financial year to the Minister of Finance for presentation to His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan for the approval of His Majesty.\n\n(2) A copy of the draft estimates prepared by the Standing Finance Committee for submission to the Council shall be delivered to each member of the Council not less than seven days before the date fixed for the meeting of the Council convened for the purpose of approving such estimates.\n\n(3) The Council may in its discretion approve, modify or reject all or any of the items appearing in such draft estimates or refer any item back to the Standing Finance Committee for its consideration or add any item thereto."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"The Council may from time to time approve supplementary Supple· estimates as may be required for any financial year for presentation mentary Estimates. to His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan, through the Minister of Finance, for the approval of His Majesty, showing the sources, if any, from which any part of the supplementary estimates may be met."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38."},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Council shall not incur any expenditure which has not No been included in any approved estimates provided that, subject to the expenditure to be incurred provisions of this Constitution, the Council may transfer all or any part unless of the moneys assigned -included in the Estimates.\n\n(a) to one item of annually recurrent expenditure to another item of annually recurrent expenditure ;\n\n(b) to one item of capital expenditure to another item of capital expenditure.\n\n(2) The provisions of sub-section ( 1) shall not apply to -\n\n(a) moneys deposited with the University by any person, wherever by the conditions of such deposit any such sum has become repayable ;\n\n(b) moneys collected and credited to the Funds of the University in error ;\n\n(c) moneys payable by the University under any judgement or order of court ;\n\n(d) moneys expended by the University m instituting or defending legal proceedings ; and\n\n(e) expenditure arising out of any property or moneys referred to in section 40. Form of 39. The annual and supplementary estimates shall be prepared in such Estimates. form and shall contain such information as the Council may direct. Power of the 40. (1) The Council may on behalf of the University accept by way Council to of grant, gift, testamentary disposition or otherwise, property and accept gifts. moneys in aid of the finances of the University on such conditions as it may determine.\n\n(2) The Bursar shall keep and maintain registers of all donations to the University including the names of donors and any special conditions on which any donation may have been given. Properly given 41. All property, moneys or funds given for any specific purposes for specific shall be applied and administered in accordance with the purposes for purposes to be which they may have been given and shall be separately accounted for . separately accounted for. Form of 42. Any contract involving the expenditure by the University of contracts. more than five hundred dollars shall be in writing, signed on behalf of the University by a person acting under the expressed or implied authority of the University ; Provided that any contract (other than a contract referred to in subsection (2) of section 54) involving expenditure by the University of more than ten thousand dollars, and any contract which if made between private persons would be required by law to be under seal shall be executed by affixing thereto the common seal of the University. Dividends 43. No dividend or bonus shall be paid and no gift or division of prohibited. money shall be made by or on behalf of the University to or among any of its members except by way of prize, reward or special grant or as part of the terms and conditions of service of staff of the University. Audit. 44. (1) The accounts of the University shall be audited annually by auditors appointed by the Council.\n\n(2) The audited accounts, with any observation made thereon by the auditors, shall be presented to the Minister of Finance.\n\nSTUDENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY Admission of 45. A student shall not be admitted to any course of study in the students. University unless he has satisfied the entry requirements prescribed for the course of study."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A46","no":46,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 46."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The registered students of the University, other than external Students' students or non-graduating students or postgraduate diploma students Association or higher degree students, shall constitute a body to be known as and Students' Representative Universiti Brunei Darussalam Students' Association (hereinafter in this Council. Constitution referred to as \"the Students' Association\").\n\n(2) The Students' Association, its constituent bodies and student bodies shall be governed and administered in accordance with the provisions prescribed by statute or regulations or their respective constitution provided that no such constitution or amendment thereof shall come into force unless and until approved by the Council.\n\n(3) The Council may impose and collect from the registered students and any other class of students such fees as the Vice-Chancellor may determine for the benefit of the Students' Association and its constituent bodies, and the fees may be applied in such manner as the Council thinks fit for the purpose of the Students' Association and its constituent bodies.\n\n(4) For the purpose of this section \"registered student\" means a student who is following a full-time course leading to a first degree or a diploma, not being a postgraduate diploma, or a certificate of the University provided that a student shall cease to be a registered student for the purpose of this section if he has passed the final examination of his course for graduation unless the Vice-Chancellor authorises in writing that such student, if he is a member of the Students' Representative Council (hereinafter referred to as the \"SRC\"). may continue to be a registered student within the meaning of this section until the election of a new SRC in the following academic year or for such lesser period as th e Vice-Chancellor may determine."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A47","no":47,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 47."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"(1) Notwithstanding section 46, it shall be lawful for not less than Establishment ten registered students of the University, with the prior approval of of other the Council and subject to such terms and conditions as the Council student bodies. may specify, to establish a student body consisting of students of the University for the promotion of a specific object or interest within the University.\n\n(2) The Council may, on the advice of the Vice-Chancellor, ruquire any such student body established under this section to be affiliated to the Students' Association subject to such terms and conditions as the Council may specify."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A48","no":48,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 48."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"If a student of the University conducts himself in a manner which, Acts by in the opinion of the Vice-Chance llor, is detrimental or prejudicial to students the well-being or reputation of the University or acts in contravention against the constitu tion of the constitution or any statute or regulation of the University, the statute, or student shall be liable to such disciplinary punishment as may be regulation of the Universit y. determined by the Vice-Chancellor or under the disciplinary regulations of the University . Acts by 49. If the Students' Association or the SRC or a student body esstudent bodies tablished under section 47 conducts itself in a manner which, in the ultra vires opinion of the Vice-Chancellor, is detrimental or prejudicial to the welltheir own constitution, being or reputation of the University or acts in contravention of the and the constitution of the University or its own constitution or any statute or Constitution, regulation of the University, the Vice-Chancellor may suspend and the statute, or regulation of Council may, on the advice of the Vice-Chancellor, dissolve the Stuthe University. dents' Association or the SRC or the student body, as the case may be ; and every office-bearer of the SRC or the said student body, as the case may be, shall be liable to such disciplinary punishment as the Council may determine or under the disciplinary regulations of the University. Suspension 50. 11) Where a student of the University is charged with a criminal and expulsion offence, he shall immediately thereupon be suspended from being a of a student student of the University. charged with a criminal offence or 12) Where a court finds that a charge for a criminal offence is against whom proved against a student of the University, the student shall immea criminal offence is diately thereupon cease to be a student of the University. proved. 13) The Vice-Chancellor may in his absolute discretion, at any time and in any particular case, exempt a student from the application of the provisions of sub-section 11) or 12), as the case may be, either unconditionally or upon such terms and conditions or for such period as the Vice-Chancellor deems fit. Disciplinary 51. 11) The disciplinary authority of the University in respect of every authority in student of the University shall be the Deputy Vice-Chancellor or, if respect of there are more than one Deputy Vice-Chancellor, such one of them students. as may be named by the Vice-Chancellor. 12) The Deputy Vice-Chancellor, who is the disciplinary authority under sub-section 11), may delegate any of his disciplinary functions, powers or duties to a board of members of the staff or officers of the University or to any member of the staff or officer of the University provided that the Deputy Vice-Chancellor shall have the power to review, rescind or vary any decision or finding of such board or staff member or officer of the University delegated with such disciplinary functions, powers or duties.\n\nGENERAL PROVISIONS Convocation. 52. 11) A Convocation for the conferment of degrees shall be held annually, or as often as the Chancellor may direct, on such date as may be approved by the Chancellor. 12) In the absence of the Chancellor or of a Pro-Chancellor who is authorised for this purpose by the Chancellor, the Vice-Chancellor shall preside over a Convocation.\n\n(3) The Procedure of Convocation shall be prescribed by statute."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A53","no":53,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 53."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"( 1) Subject to sub-section (4), the disciplinary authority of the Disciplinary University in respect of every member of the staff of the University provisions and shall be the Disciplinary Committee of the University which shall con-disciplinary authority in sist of : respect of staff of the University.\n\n(a) two members of the Council elected by the Council, one of whom shall be appointed by the Council as Chairman ; and\n\n(b) the Vice-Chancellor.\n\n(2) In the exercise of its disciplinary functions, the Disciplinary Committee shall have the power to take such disciplinary action and impose such disciplinary punishment as may be provided for under any statute or regulations.\n\n(3) The Disciplinary Committee may delegate any of its disciplinary functions, powers or duties to any member of the staff or officers of the University or any board of members of staff or officers of the University, in respect of any particular member of the staff or officer of the University or in respect of any class or category of members of the staff or officers of the University provided that :\n\n(a) the member of the staff or officer of the University or the board delegated with such functions, powers or duties shall carry out, exercise and discharge the functions, powers or duties under the direction and control of the Disciplinary Committee which shall have the power to review rescind of vary any decision or finding of such member of the staff or officer or such board ; and\n\n(b) no delegation shall be made under this sub-section as to enable a member of the staff or officer of the University to exercise any disciplinary authority or to be a member of a board which may exercise any disciplinary authority over a member of the staff or officer who is superior to him in rank.\n\n(4) The Disciplinary Committee shall have no jurisdiction in respect of the Chancellor, the Pro-Chancellor or the Vice-Chancellor.\n\n(5) Any member of the staff of the University who is dissatisfied with the decision of the disciplinary authority mentioned in this section may appeal against such decision to the University Council which may give such decision thereon as it deems fit and proper. Appointments 54. (1) All persons employed or to be employed by the University of teachers other than those mentioned in sections 9 and 10 shall, subject to the and employees provisions of this Constitution, be appointed by the Council.\n\n(2) Every person employed by the University shall, subject to the provisions of this Constitution or any statute or regulations, hold office on such terms and conditions as may be prescribed by the Council and the terms and conditions to be so prescribed shall be deemed to include a prOVISIOn\n\n(a) in relation to teaching, examining, invigilating and other similar duties, that his employment is subject to the provisions of this Constitution and to the provisions of all statutes and regulations as from time to time amended : and\n\n(b) in relation to all other terms and conditions of service that his employment is subject to the provisions of this Constitution and to the provisions of all statutes and regulations in force on the date of the commencement of his employment.\n\n(3) Nothing in this section shall prevent the Council from entermg into a special contractual arrangement with a person to be so employed by the University if it is in the opinion of the Council expedient so to do. All 55. Notwithstanding the provisions of section 54 or any other proappointments visions of this Constitution, every person employed by the University to be subject shall hold office subject to the provisions of the Order and any subto the Order and any sidiary legislation made thereunder and the terms and conditions of subsidiary their employment or appointments shall be deemed to include a provithereunder. le~islation sion to this effect. Powers of 56. ( 1) Where by the provisions of this Constitution or any statute delegation. or regulation any officer or body is empowered to exercise any power or perform any duty, such officer or body may be instrument in writing subject to the provisions of this section and to such conditions and restrictions as may be prescribed in such instrument, delegate the exercise of such powers or the performance of such duties to any body or to any committee or to any person described therein by name or office.\n\n(2) A delegation under this section may be revoked at any time by the officer or body making such delegation.\n\n(3) No delegation of any power or duty under this section shall affect the exercise of such power or the performance .of such duty by the officer or body making such delegation.\n\n(4) Nothing in this section shall apply to any power to make or approve statutes or regulations."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A57","no":57,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 57."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"If any member of an authority, or any graduate of the Univer-Deprivation of sity, or any person who has received a diploma or other academic dis-degree, etc. on tinction from the University, is convicted by a court of law of any grounds of misconduct. heinous offence whether within or without Brunei Darussalam, or is in the opinion of the Council guilty of scandalous conduct, it shall be lawful for the Chancellor, on the recommendation of not less than twothirds of all the members of the Council -\n\n(a) to remove him from membership of the authority ; or\n\n(b) to deprive him of any degree, diploma or other academic distinction conferred upon him by the University."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A58","no":58,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 58."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VII"},"text":{"en":"If any question arises whether any person has been duly elect-Disputes as to ed, appointed, nominated or co-opted to membership or is entitled to elections be or to remain a member of any authority or other body in the determined by the University, the question shall be referred to the Chancellor, whose de-Chancellor. cision thereon shall be final.\n\nTRANSITIONAL PROVISIONS"}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A59","no":59,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 59."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VIII"},"text":{"en":"Notwithstanding the provisions of sub-section (1) of section The first Vice· 9, the person holding the office of Vice-Chancellor of the University Chancellor immediately before the appointed day, shall continue to be the ViceChancellor of the University established under the Order upon the same terms and conditions as were applicable to him immediately before the appointed day and shall hold office at the pleasure of His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A60","no":60,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 60."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VIII"},"text":{"en":"Notwithstanding the provisions of sub-section (1) of section Existing 10, the person holding or acting in the office of Deputy Vice-Chancellor holder of post of Deputy immediately prior to the appointed day shall be deemed as having been Vice· appointed to or acting in the post of Deputy Vice-Chancellor of the Chancellor. University established under the Order, as the case may be, upon the same terms and conditions as were applicable to the holder immediately before the appointed day, and shall hold office at the pleasure of His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan."}},{"id":"BN-S-20-1988-E-EMERGENCY-UNIVERSITI-BRUNEI-DARUSSALAM-ORDER-1988-A61","no":61,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 61."},"chapter":{"en":"PART VIII"},"text":{"en":"Notwithstanding the provisions of section 11, the person holding Existing the office of Registrar-cum-Bursar, or Chief Librarian or Bursar immedi-holder of post of Registrar· . , · ately before the appointed day shall be deemed as having been appoint-cum-Bursar, ed to the post of Registrar and Secretary or Chief Libra~ian or Bursar Chief Librarian or respectively under this Constitution upon the same terms and condi-Bursar. tions as were applicable to him immediately before the appointed day. Existing Deans 62. Notwithstanding the provisions of sub-section (1) of section of Faculties. 19, a person who has been appointed as the Dean of a Faculty immediately before the appointed day shall be deemed to have been appointed under this Constitution and shall continue to hold such office for a period not exceeding two years from the date of his appointment as Dean unless he shall by writing, earlier resign his office or is removed earlier from such office by the Council of the Board of Management referred to in sub-section (1) of section 67. Succession to 63. (1) Subject to the provisions of this section and to any direction property, etc. of the Council, all property and assets vested in the University or any other person on its behalf immediately before the appointed day shall on that day vest in the University established under this Constitution.\n\n(2) Any land which immediately before the appointed day was vested in the University shall on that day vest in the University established under this Constitution. Continuance 64. Subject to the provisions of this Constitution, all persons who of agreements immediately before the appointed day were employed by or on behalf of service, etc. of the University shall on that day be deemed to be employed by the University established under the Order and this Constitution upon the same terms and conditions as were applicable to them before that day. Transitional 65. (1) Until a seal is provided pursuant to the provisions of section provision 6, a stamp bearing the inscription \"Universiti Brunei Darussalam\" may relating to University be used and shall be deemed for the purposes of such section to be seal. the common seal of the University.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding the provisions_ of sub-section (3) of section 6, unti.l the Council is constituted in accordance with section 15 the signature of only the Vice-Chancellor on any instrument bearing the seal referred to in sub-section ( 1) shall be sufficient evidence that such seal was duly and properly affixed and that the same is the lawful seal of the University. Transitional 66. Notwithstanding the provisions of section 46, the Students' provision Association and the Students' Representative Council existing in the relating to the Students' University immediately prior to the appointed day shall be deemed to Association be the Students' Association and the Students' Representative Council and the of the University constituted under this Constitution. Students' Representative Council. Transitional 67. (1) Notwithstanding the provisions of sub-section (1) of sections provisions 15 and 17 in respect of the Council and the Senate, the following tranrelating to the Council and sitional provisions shall apply until such time as the Council and the Senate. Senate are duly constituted under this Constitution, that is to say -\n\n(a) the functions and powers of the Council shall be exercised by a Board of Management consisting of :\n\n(i) the Vice Chancellor as Chairman ;\n\n(ii) the Deputy Minister of Education as the Deputy Chairman;\n\n(iii) the Attorney General (or his representative) ;\n\n(iv) the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Education (or his representative) ;\n\n(v) the Permanent Secretary , Ministry of Finance (or his representative) ;\n\n(vi) The Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Development (or his representative) ;\n\n(vii) the Permanent Secretary, Ministry or Religious Affairs (or his representative) ;\n\n(viii) the Director of Establishment (or his representative) ;\n\n(ix) one person elected by the Academic Board from among its members other than the Vice-Chancellor or the Deputy Vice-Chancellor ;\n\n(x) such other persons as may be appointed by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan ; and\n\n(xi) the Registrar and Secretary as Secretary .\n\n(b) the functions and powers of the Senate shall be exercised by an Academic Board consisting of :\n\n(i) the Vice-Chancellor as Chairman ;\n\n(ii) the Deputy Vice-Chancellor as Deputy Chairman,\n\n(iii) the Academic Adviser of the University ;\n\n(iv) the Deans ;\n\n(v) the head~ of the teaching departments of a Faculty ;\n\n(vi) the professors of the University but not including visiting professors ;\n\n(vii) the Chief Librarian ;\n\n(viii) the Bursar ; and\n\n(ix) the Registrar and Secretary as Secretary.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding the provison of sub-section (1), the persons appointed by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan by name to be members of the Board of Management existing in the University immediately prior to the appointed day shall be deemed to have been appointed under paragraph (a)(x) of sub-section (1) as members of the Board of Management constituted under this section. · Transitional 68. Notwithstanding the provisions of section 18, the Faculties provisions existing in the University immediately prior to the appointed day shall relating to the be deemed to the Faculties constituted under this Constitution. Faculties. Made this 25th day of April, 1988 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN BRUNEI DARUSSALAM."}}],"pack":"bn-p14","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"EMERGENCY UNIVERSITI BRUNEI DARUSSALAM ORDER 1988","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
